WEBVTT


00:37.170 --> 00:41.280
I'll see you later, Eren.

00:50.890 --> 00:53.440
Huh? Mikasa...

00:53.870 --> 00:55.680
Let's head back.

00:55.680 --> 00:58.160
What am I doing here?

00:58.160 --> 01:00.980
You're so out of it. Were you sound asleep?

01:00.980 --> 01:02.360
No...

01:02.360 --> 01:06.290
It's just, I feel like I had a really long dream.

01:07.910 --> 01:09.730
What was it about?

01:10.310 --> 01:12.360
I can't remember...

01:14.350 --> 01:15.370
Eren,

01:15.810 --> 01:17.520
why are you crying?

01:23.630 --> 01:25.710
CHAPTER 1

01:25.710 --> 01:33.650
CHAPTER 1
THE RUMBLING

01:38.700 --> 01:43.900
Listen, Halil. Me and you are the only ones
who know where this is.

01:44.300 --> 01:47.760
I'm gonna stash money here
until this sack is full.

01:47.760 --> 01:52.780
Then we'll have enough for everyone
to be able to live someplace nice.

01:53.550 --> 01:57.420
But, Ramzi, if you keep this up...

01:57.420 --> 02:00.290
someday you'll lose your left hand, too.

02:01.070 --> 02:04.240
You shouldn't make Grandpa any sadder.

02:05.170 --> 02:08.130
But someone has to do this.

02:08.860 --> 02:12.530
With all of us stuck in those shabby tents,

02:12.530 --> 02:14.640
more and more people will die every year

02:14.640 --> 02:16.950
because they couldn't survive the winter.

02:17.880 --> 02:23.220
So, Halil, if I die, please give
this money to everyone for me.

02:23.790 --> 02:25.140
Ramzi...

02:27.940 --> 02:29.240
Hide it!

02:31.720 --> 02:33.130
What's going on?

02:33.130 --> 02:36.580
The townspeople are... fleeing?

02:38.620 --> 02:39.750
Why?

03:08.890 --> 03:12.450
In the future, though
I'm not sure exactly how far,

03:13.550 --> 03:16.230
I massacre these people.

03:17.910 --> 03:19.910
Before too long, they'll all die.

03:21.020 --> 03:24.380
No, I kill them.

03:26.060 --> 03:28.420
It's already determined that I do.

03:29.830 --> 03:36.690
I imagine no one ever found a way
for Paradis Island to survive.

03:37.780 --> 03:39.910
Everything here will be gone.

03:41.680 --> 03:43.380
The homes,

03:43.380 --> 03:45.110
the people,

03:45.110 --> 03:47.000
the animals,

03:47.000 --> 03:48.360
people's lives,

03:48.940 --> 03:50.210
their dreams...

03:56.120 --> 03:59.030
What would Mom think?

03:59.870 --> 04:04.270
Shouldn't we Eldians be the ones to die?

04:05.590 --> 04:08.630
In the same way the King of the walls
chose the path to humanity's downfall?

04:09.420 --> 04:11.920
At the very least,
the death toll on the island

04:11.920 --> 04:14.220
would be but a fraction
of that of the rest of the world.

04:15.180 --> 04:20.870
It's also true that if Eldians completely
die out, the Titan problem goes away.

04:23.060 --> 04:27.770
I just can't accept things ending that way...

04:30.980 --> 04:32.270
This scene...

04:33.590 --> 04:35.810
I've seen it in memories of the future.

04:37.120 --> 04:38.780
Most likely,

04:39.400 --> 04:41.530
I save this kid.

04:48.330 --> 04:52.250
This kid's a foreign refugee
and a serial pickpocket.

04:52.250 --> 04:55.050
And since this is where we do business,

04:55.050 --> 04:57.800
we're just doing a little pest control here.

04:57.800 --> 05:01.430
This ain't got nothin' to do
with you. Get lost.

05:02.140 --> 05:05.190
Yeah... That's true.

05:07.690 --> 05:10.190
What am I thinking?

05:10.770 --> 05:13.310
I eventually kill this kid, too.

05:14.070 --> 05:15.700
Who do I think I am?

05:18.280 --> 05:19.570
Take this!

05:19.570 --> 05:22.320
I've committed horrible acts of violence.

05:22.320 --> 05:24.870
I have no business acting
like a righteous person.

05:33.540 --> 05:36.970
It appears the future doesn't change.

05:37.250 --> 05:38.260
Thanks!

05:40.220 --> 05:42.550
I'm the same as you, Reiner.

05:43.220 --> 05:45.280
A half-assed piece of shit.

05:47.350 --> 05:49.100
No, that's wrong.

05:49.100 --> 05:50.600
I'm worse than that.

05:51.350 --> 05:52.520
I'm sorry.

05:53.350 --> 05:56.780
I'm sorry. I'm so sorry.

05:57.780 --> 06:00.030
Why're you crying?

06:00.530 --> 06:03.030
Ramzi! Halil!

06:03.030 --> 06:05.410
Hurry! Come with us!

06:05.410 --> 06:06.540
Ramzi!

06:09.290 --> 06:11.290
Run! Run!

06:11.290 --> 06:12.750
Why are there Titans?!

06:12.750 --> 06:13.790
The mountains!

06:13.790 --> 06:15.300
Head for higher ground!

06:15.300 --> 06:17.800
It's no use! Look there!

06:17.800 --> 06:19.880
The Titans are in the mountains too!

06:19.880 --> 06:20.800
No...

06:20.800 --> 06:22.800
We're done for!

06:22.800 --> 06:24.810
There's nowhere to escape to!

06:24.810 --> 06:27.680
Did the Marleyans flee without warning us?

06:27.680 --> 06:29.810
They're too fast!

06:30.230 --> 06:35.360
Ramzi, are we gonna get
stepped on and crushed?

06:37.440 --> 06:39.990
That's not gonna happen! Don't give up!

06:42.820 --> 06:46.660
To save the island... To save Eldia...

06:47.450 --> 06:49.660
But there's... more to this...

07:02.420 --> 07:03.710
The money!

07:03.710 --> 07:04.430
Halil!

07:05.180 --> 07:07.470
The reality of the world outside the walls

07:08.080 --> 07:11.930
was different from the world I dreamed of...

07:14.610 --> 07:16.070
Halil!

07:20.480 --> 07:24.290
It was different from the world
I saw in Armin's book.

07:26.100 --> 07:30.580
When I learned humanity
was alive outside the walls,

07:32.910 --> 07:33.920
I...

07:36.000 --> 07:38.120
was disappointed.

07:42.880 --> 07:46.130
I... wanted this...

07:50.380 --> 07:54.270
I wanted... to wipe everything away...

07:57.240 --> 08:00.370
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

08:01.770 --> 08:02.980
I'm sorry.

08:14.440 --> 08:16.380
I'm so sorry!

08:29.300 --> 08:31.600
Come on! Open the gate! Please!

09:07.840 --> 09:10.760
Hello? Is somebody there?

09:10.760 --> 09:12.390
Anybody!

09:15.900 --> 09:17.020
Dear.

09:18.140 --> 09:22.350
It's here, isn't it?
Judgment day has come for us.

10:47.490 --> 10:49.400
From the moment I was born,

10:50.030 --> 10:53.150
there was always a stifling wall before me.

10:54.830 --> 10:56.330
Fiery water,

10:57.040 --> 10:58.540
lands of ice,

10:59.160 --> 11:00.660
sandy snowfields...

11:09.410 --> 11:11.460
The people who witnessed these things

11:17.310 --> 11:20.640
were the ones that had obtained
the greatest freedom in the world.

11:26.940 --> 11:28.230
This...

11:31.690 --> 11:33.230
is freedom!

11:39.200 --> 11:44.380
We've finally made it here to see this.

11:53.880 --> 11:55.390
Haven't we, Armin?

12:01.450 --> 12:02.390
Eren...

12:03.170 --> 12:05.400
Are your wounds healed now?

12:05.980 --> 12:08.400
Huh? Annie?

12:11.140 --> 12:14.370
Yeah, since we've had some time...

12:14.370 --> 12:19.950
I never imagined we'd be able
to relax like this.

12:23.740 --> 12:25.670
Wanna sit with me?

12:31.670 --> 12:35.640
I've... been meaning to thank you.

12:35.640 --> 12:36.640
Huh?

12:37.220 --> 12:40.050
For coming to talk to me for years.

12:41.550 --> 12:42.680
So thank you.

12:43.970 --> 12:45.690
Oh. Yeah.

12:46.400 --> 12:49.900
I was so lonely I thought I'd go crazy.

12:49.900 --> 12:53.690
Hearing from you and Hitch
was the only joy I had.

12:54.450 --> 12:55.410
Annie...

12:55.410 --> 13:01.320
But why did you choose to spend time
chatting with a rock that never responded?

13:02.660 --> 13:06.580
There were more cheerful and
pleasant girls to talk to, right?

13:07.750 --> 13:11.080
That's... not how I felt.

13:12.790 --> 13:15.720
It was because I wanted to see you, Annie.

13:24.180 --> 13:25.440
How come?

13:26.020 --> 13:28.480
What? You really don't know?

13:28.480 --> 13:30.810
After how much Hitch teased me?

13:33.480 --> 13:34.990
I don't know.

13:41.700 --> 13:45.500
What am I even doing?

13:46.040 --> 13:49.250
Right now, thousands,
if not hundreds of millions,

13:49.250 --> 13:54.000
are being trampled to death all
across the world, and we're...

13:58.590 --> 14:00.010
I know.

14:00.430 --> 14:05.140
You were talking to an enemy like me
because you're a good person. Right?

14:05.730 --> 14:09.020
For the same reason you won't give up
on talking things out with Eren.

14:09.640 --> 14:11.520
I could have woken up at any moment.

14:12.060 --> 14:16.030
Talking to the monster was
another way to avoid a conflict.

14:16.700 --> 14:18.030
Right?

14:32.460 --> 14:33.870
Don't go.

14:35.340 --> 14:38.510
Also, I told you this before, but...

14:38.510 --> 14:41.130
I really do hate the phrase "good person."

14:42.720 --> 14:45.310
I killed a huge number of people.

14:45.310 --> 14:48.520
Including civilians... Even children...

14:49.180 --> 14:54.690
And now I've made a choice that
betrays the people of my island,

14:54.690 --> 14:56.650
and killed friends as a result.

14:57.530 --> 14:59.820
I've long since become a monster, too.

15:01.150 --> 15:03.900
Some part of me thought that, one day,

15:03.900 --> 15:07.660
the promise Eren and I made to
explore the unknown world together

15:09.080 --> 15:11.330
would become a reality.

15:12.830 --> 15:16.260
The unknown world wasn't what
it was cracked up to be, right?

15:16.920 --> 15:21.670
Yeah. It was different from
the world we'd dreamed of.

15:22.880 --> 15:24.170
But...

15:33.560 --> 15:39.190
I want to believe there must
still be something beyond the walls

15:39.780 --> 15:41.440
that we don't know about.

15:55.210 --> 15:56.880
Quiet, isn't it?

15:56.880 --> 16:00.500
The residents of Odiha
must have already fled south,

16:00.500 --> 16:03.130
seeing as how every ship is gone.

16:03.590 --> 16:07.680
Well, then, we're in
the Azumabito clan's hands.

16:07.680 --> 16:12.220
Yes, and we shall do whatever it takes
to launch the flying boat into the air.

16:13.260 --> 16:14.610
Remove the cover!

16:14.610 --> 16:15.570
Hurry!

16:15.570 --> 16:18.230
Dammit! These explosives are in the way.

16:18.230 --> 16:19.480
Let's cut 'em off and toss 'em.

16:19.480 --> 16:20.570
Wait.

16:21.150 --> 16:25.580
We might be able to use them.
Let's load them on the flying boat.

16:29.370 --> 16:32.080
How can that be?!

16:32.450 --> 16:34.670
They're all dead?

16:34.670 --> 16:38.460
Commander Magath... My family
in Liberio... All of them?!

16:39.130 --> 16:43.340
The rumbling has already destroyed
a majority of the continent of Marley.

16:43.340 --> 16:45.470
Then what do we do now?

16:45.470 --> 16:49.640
What will we do? There's nobody else!

16:54.010 --> 16:57.150
I'm sorry. I don't know.

16:59.230 --> 17:02.440
Annie, check your equipment.

17:03.060 --> 17:06.200
You're still not used to
the new ODM gear, are you?

17:06.870 --> 17:09.740
Go with Reiner and zip around
over there to get accustomed.

17:12.820 --> 17:13.740
Why?

17:15.790 --> 17:20.420
We should... do the things we can... so...

17:20.420 --> 17:23.130
I believe I told you that I'm backing out.

17:24.000 --> 17:26.390
You don't even intend to get
on the flying boat either?

17:28.010 --> 17:30.720
Sorry, but I'm staying behind.

17:32.300 --> 17:38.310
Wanting to save humanity...
I don't really get that.

17:39.330 --> 17:45.910
If anything, us Eldians in Marley were
persecuted by the "humanity" you want to save

17:45.910 --> 17:48.070
from the moment we were born.

17:48.740 --> 17:52.110
Even if hypothetically
the rumbling stopped now,

17:52.110 --> 17:54.360
with Marley gone,

17:54.360 --> 17:58.170
there's no one left to protect the Eldians.

18:01.210 --> 18:03.420
I truly do feel sorry about this,

18:03.920 --> 18:06.430
when they're putting everything

18:06.430 --> 18:08.760
toward the slim hope
of saving their homeland.

18:10.630 --> 18:14.010
But... I can't fight anymore.

18:15.390 --> 18:17.310
I want to spend the time I have left

18:18.470 --> 18:20.940
living peacefully.

18:30.850 --> 18:32.250
When did this happen?

18:33.490 --> 18:35.160
When did what happen?

18:35.160 --> 18:37.290
Okay. I get it.

18:37.290 --> 18:38.460
Get what?

18:40.660 --> 18:44.590
You don't have to suffer anymore.

18:46.630 --> 18:53.220
But... Armin is going to board
the flying boat with us and head for Eren.

18:56.230 --> 18:57.480
I know.

19:00.100 --> 19:03.140
What about you? What do you want?

19:03.680 --> 19:07.240
Are you gonna go kill Eren to save humanity?

19:09.240 --> 19:10.240
I won't kill him.

19:11.440 --> 19:14.110
Eren's gone far away,
and I'm bringing him back.

19:14.110 --> 19:16.750
That's all I'm doing.

19:18.840 --> 19:20.370
By the way,

19:21.120 --> 19:22.750
did you lose your scarf?

19:25.170 --> 19:26.260
I have it.

19:31.760 --> 19:34.770
This is crazy! You should still be in bed!

19:35.140 --> 19:37.640
Stay in bed?

19:37.640 --> 19:43.600
If I lie down any longer, you shits
are gonna forget all about me.

19:43.600 --> 19:50.110
And that bearded bitch who passed out
after her arm was broken is awake.

19:50.110 --> 19:52.780
I'll be damned if we don't make her
tell us where Eren's going.

19:55.580 --> 19:59.540
Assuming a global combined fleet
sets out to attack Paradis Island,

20:00.370 --> 20:03.040
it would gather here at Karifa Naval Port.

20:03.580 --> 20:05.050
After the raid on Liberio,

20:05.420 --> 20:09.630
we'll give them a month's time
to rally the global alliance,

20:09.630 --> 20:13.050
then you'll gain control of the Founding
Titan by making contact with Zeke

20:13.550 --> 20:15.810
and activate a limited rumbling.

20:16.600 --> 20:20.060
The several hundred Titans in the
Shiganshina section of the outer wall

20:20.060 --> 20:22.350
should be able to take them out with ease.

20:22.930 --> 20:25.320
Is that the only target?

20:26.320 --> 20:30.320
Will that be enough to keep Paradis
Island untouched for decades?

20:30.900 --> 20:34.740
A nation that loses its fleet
will be driven to economic collapse.

20:34.740 --> 20:39.330
If that happens to all the major nations,
it should be more than sufficient a blow.

20:40.030 --> 20:41.540
If I had to pick another target,

20:41.540 --> 20:44.840
it would be this fortress
in Marley's southern mountains...

20:45.210 --> 20:48.880
The airship research base here
is of some concern.

20:52.880 --> 20:57.600
Most likely, that is
Eren's second target.

20:58.640 --> 21:00.510
Fort Salta...

21:01.010 --> 21:03.720
True. If he knew of the existence of weapons

21:03.720 --> 21:06.560
that had the slightest chance
of harming the Founding Titan...

21:07.150 --> 21:10.020
I expect that's his next stop
after Karifa Naval Port.

21:10.730 --> 21:12.810
He'll go to destroy the airships.

21:14.820 --> 21:17.550
You answered mighty obediently.

21:18.320 --> 21:20.820
I have a request for all of you.

21:22.320 --> 21:24.370
Please acknowledge something.

21:24.370 --> 21:28.580
Zeke was defeated. But he was right.

21:29.380 --> 21:33.380
The only solution to the
two-millennium-spanning Eldian problem

21:33.380 --> 21:36.090
was the euthanization plan.

21:36.890 --> 21:39.510
I'm sure you can see that
in the wake of this disaster.

21:40.470 --> 21:42.590
Yeah. I admit it.

21:43.800 --> 21:46.230
I wasn't able to show Eren any solution,

21:46.600 --> 21:49.270
or hope, or a future.

21:49.900 --> 21:51.730
I admit my powerlessness.

21:57.910 --> 22:00.110
This is all the fuel we have on the ship.

22:00.110 --> 22:01.860
Go ahead and leave it there.

22:14.580 --> 22:16.470
Please take those two with you.

22:17.050 --> 22:20.970
Being on the ship won't
really guarantee their safety.

22:21.680 --> 22:23.880
But it's better than taking them
on the flying boat.

22:24.430 --> 22:29.140
I don't mind doing so, of course,
but will they accept that?

22:29.140 --> 22:31.390
I'll confine them in their cabin.

22:31.980 --> 22:34.640
Don't let them out until
the flying boat takes off.

22:35.570 --> 22:37.030
What about you?

22:37.400 --> 22:40.110
I have to repay my fallen comrades.

22:40.820 --> 22:42.900
I'll perform my role as a Warrior.

22:55.720 --> 22:57.010
Hange!

22:57.010 --> 23:00.300
In about an hour, we can
begin preparations for takeoff!

23:00.300 --> 23:01.420
Got it!

23:02.590 --> 23:06.680
You heard the man.
Each of you, inspect your gear.

23:07.270 --> 23:08.180
Yes, Commander!

23:14.520 --> 23:18.690
Two fingers is all I need. I'm ready.

23:19.820 --> 23:22.780
So I'm the only one running away...

23:22.780 --> 23:24.150
Don't worry about it.

23:25.100 --> 23:28.550
From the beginning, you were
never subservient to Marley.

23:29.080 --> 23:31.580
You don't have to shoulder anything more.

23:33.500 --> 23:36.590
All this time, I've wanted to apologize

23:37.260 --> 23:39.380
to you and Bertholdt.

23:39.380 --> 23:41.260
It all goes back to that day,

23:41.260 --> 23:44.090
when I continued the mission
that started all this.

23:44.670 --> 23:47.600
That day, if I had turned back,

23:48.140 --> 23:53.220
both you and Bertholdt could have
gone home and seen your families.

23:55.030 --> 23:58.030
It feels presumptuous to even apologize.

23:59.230 --> 24:03.860
Yeah. I don't know how many times
I decided to kill you, only to stop myself.

24:05.870 --> 24:08.870
I'm glad you didn't.

24:15.050 --> 24:16.880
Take care of Gabi and Falco.

24:18.170 --> 24:19.880
Understood.

24:23.750 --> 24:25.640
Annie!

24:25.640 --> 24:27.720
Annie, take care!

24:27.720 --> 24:28.890
See you later!

24:39.570 --> 24:42.020
Armin, are you all right with this?

24:42.770 --> 24:43.900
With what?

24:44.270 --> 24:47.910
To be honest, I was relying on her.

24:47.910 --> 24:50.910
But Annie has fought enough.

24:52.160 --> 24:54.490
I am. I...

24:55.500 --> 24:58.340
I want Annie to stay Annie.

25:00.090 --> 25:02.670
Are you two sure you want to come with us?

25:02.670 --> 25:07.430
Assuming the rumbling stops, Eldians won't
find themselves in a great position...

25:07.430 --> 25:12.720
I hate to admit it,
but you were right, Hange.

25:12.720 --> 25:16.560
General Magath was leaving us a final order:

25:17.440 --> 25:21.230
to work together
and do what needs to be done.

25:22.190 --> 25:23.360
Pieck.

25:23.940 --> 25:28.030
I'd love to ride on the Cart Titan's back
sometime and feel its body heat as we—

25:28.030 --> 25:29.490
No.

25:29.490 --> 25:31.450
That took a sudden, creepy turn.

25:34.120 --> 25:38.420
I see your love of Titans is
still unrequited, four-eyes.

25:38.420 --> 25:40.460
We'll be pals soon enough.

25:46.300 --> 25:50.220
Tell me, Levi.
Do you think they're all watching?

25:51.800 --> 25:56.980
You think we can stand proud before
our fallen comrades as we are now?

25:58.810 --> 26:01.980
Don't go and start sounding like him.

26:05.530 --> 26:08.240
Good. Begin the fueling process!

26:08.740 --> 26:10.030
Yes, sir.

26:10.740 --> 26:12.110
Thank goodness.

26:12.110 --> 26:15.330
We're gonna make it before
the rumbling gets here.

26:42.060 --> 26:43.640
Floch...

26:44.060 --> 26:47.240
Don't tell me you clung to
the ship all the way here—

26:47.240 --> 26:48.150
Hange!

26:50.070 --> 26:52.400
There are holes in the fuel tank!

26:57.160 --> 26:58.960
We can't fly like this!

26:58.960 --> 27:00.000
Don't lose hope.

27:00.750 --> 27:03.160
If we seal the holes, we can make it work!

27:03.910 --> 27:05.170
Get the welding tools!

27:07.630 --> 27:09.170
How long will it take?

27:09.760 --> 27:13.550
With tin plates, we could
do it in an hour, barely.

27:21.270 --> 27:23.060
This sound...

27:24.640 --> 27:25.570
Don't tell me...

27:28.400 --> 27:29.570
It's here.

27:30.740 --> 27:33.490
The rumbling... is here.

27:35.620 --> 27:37.830
Don't do it.

27:38.370 --> 27:41.830
Please.... don't...

27:42.540 --> 27:43.580
Floch...

27:43.580 --> 27:44.790
Be ready to start fueling at any moment!

27:44.790 --> 27:49.840
Every...one... on the...
island... will be... killed...

27:50.460 --> 27:54.840
Our devils...

27:56.020 --> 27:58.350
are our...

27:59.020 --> 28:02.600
only... hope...

28:04.350 --> 28:06.480
Come on! Floch!

28:06.480 --> 28:07.860
He's dead.

28:09.030 --> 28:13.610
It's as you said, Floch.

28:14.150 --> 28:17.080
But I just can't give up.

28:17.790 --> 28:19.370
Even if it's hopeless today,

28:20.620 --> 28:22.370
maybe someday...

28:33.880 --> 28:35.890
Why? Let us out!

28:35.890 --> 28:37.970
The Titans are on our doorstep, aren't they?

28:37.970 --> 28:39.180
- Let us out!
- Open the door!

28:39.180 --> 28:40.720
Be quiet!

28:45.480 --> 28:48.190
Armin, do you have any ideas?

28:49.440 --> 28:52.110
Only one.

28:52.110 --> 28:54.860
I stay behind and slow them down.

28:54.860 --> 28:56.530
It can't be you.

28:56.530 --> 28:59.830
You're our sole trump card
for stopping Eren.

29:00.910 --> 29:01.950
I'll do it.

29:01.950 --> 29:03.330
That's out of the question!

29:03.910 --> 29:07.840
We can't afford to expend
another shred of Titan power.

29:08.560 --> 29:11.710
I'm the one who led you this far.

29:11.710 --> 29:15.090
And we killed many friends
and comrades to get here.

29:15.680 --> 29:17.850
I'm taking responsibility for that.

29:18.450 --> 29:19.760
Hange...

29:21.760 --> 29:23.600
Armin Arlelt.

29:23.600 --> 29:27.730
I hereby designate you the 15th Commander
of the Scout Regiment.

29:29.300 --> 29:32.440
The position calls for a certain quality—

29:32.440 --> 29:35.240
a mindset of continuously
pursuing understanding.

29:36.120 --> 29:38.740
There's no one more suitable than you.

29:39.910 --> 29:41.740
I leave everyone in your hands.

29:44.320 --> 29:46.000
Well, that's that.

29:46.000 --> 29:47.460
See ya, everyone.

29:47.960 --> 29:49.290
Ah, yes.

29:49.290 --> 29:53.500
Levi's your underling now,
so really put him to work.

30:01.760 --> 30:04.010
Hey. Four-eyes.

30:05.010 --> 30:06.700
You understand, right, Levi?

30:06.700 --> 30:10.520
My turn's come at last.

30:13.020 --> 30:17.410
I have the urge to make a
supremely cool exit right now.

30:17.910 --> 30:19.910
Don't stop what I've got going.

30:29.500 --> 30:31.460
Give your heart.

30:38.130 --> 30:40.470
That's the first time
I've heard you say that.

30:41.880 --> 30:43.590
Hange!

30:56.900 --> 31:01.360
Ah, Titans truly are marvelous!

31:51.500 --> 31:54.000
The holes are sealed! Start fueling!

31:54.000 --> 31:56.260
Hurry! Hurry!

32:20.940 --> 32:22.480
They're right on top of us!

32:22.480 --> 32:25.740
There's no more time for fueling!
Start the engine!

32:29.580 --> 32:31.490
Push the fuselage forward!

32:38.000 --> 32:39.130
They need more time?!

32:42.630 --> 32:43.630
Hot!

33:00.570 --> 33:02.400
Launch the ship!

33:02.900 --> 33:03.980
Grab my hand!

33:27.720 --> 33:28.680
Hange...

33:43.310 --> 33:46.200
So long, Hange.

33:47.440 --> 33:48.650
Watch us.

34:06.470 --> 34:07.470
The flying boat!

34:09.800 --> 34:11.220
It took off.

34:12.710 --> 34:17.100
Hange, you fulfilled your role.

34:17.850 --> 34:19.520
Erwin?

34:19.520 --> 34:20.850
All of you...

34:30.200 --> 34:31.280
I see.

34:34.950 --> 34:40.500
I'm tellin' ya, I really had my hands
full after being named commander.

34:41.710 --> 34:43.620
With Eren's idiocy, that is.

34:43.620 --> 34:46.590
Yeah, you had it tough.

34:47.470 --> 34:48.880
You can tell us all about it.

34:49.800 --> 34:50.810
Yeah.

34:52.260 --> 34:54.340
CHAPTER 2

34:54.340 --> 35:02.270
CHAPTER 2
SINNERS

35:19.160 --> 35:20.540
The fuel is...

35:20.540 --> 35:23.960
Yeah. They only managed
to fill the tank halfway.

35:24.750 --> 35:27.170
Will it get us to Fort Salta?

35:28.880 --> 35:30.990
I'll make sure we reach the fortress.

35:32.490 --> 35:37.560
This flight is our last hope,
and Hange died giving it to us.

35:38.100 --> 35:42.350
I'll deliver you to that base. I swear it.

35:43.980 --> 35:48.070
So make sure you stop the rumbling,

35:49.110 --> 35:50.610
no matter what it takes.

35:51.860 --> 35:53.110
We will.

35:53.110 --> 35:55.700
We're in your hands, Onyankopon.

35:57.970 --> 35:58.950
Now, then...

35:59.750 --> 36:01.540
Let's come up with our plan.

36:03.450 --> 36:07.590
Pieck, Captain Levi, is this roughly
the shape of the Founding Titan?

36:07.590 --> 36:10.800
Yes, though I didn't get a great look at it.

36:11.300 --> 36:16.100
Basically, it's a humongous bundle
of bones that moves like an insect.

36:16.100 --> 36:20.600
If it's like a normal Titan, Eren
would be in the neck near the head.

36:20.600 --> 36:24.220
Given the War Hammer's abilities,
that's not guaranteed.

36:25.060 --> 36:29.360
In other words, we don't know
which part Eren is in.

36:29.940 --> 36:34.230
Even if we don't know where he is,
we can blast the whole thing away.

36:34.980 --> 36:38.330
The same way you annihilated Liberio's port

36:39.360 --> 36:41.810
with the Colossal Titan.

36:45.240 --> 36:49.000
That certainly would be
the most effective method.

36:50.210 --> 36:53.460
But we'll leave that for after
we've exhausted our chance to talk.

36:54.340 --> 36:57.430
If there's still no other way to stop Eren,

36:58.100 --> 36:59.760
that's our last resort.

37:02.010 --> 37:05.140
It's great to have a last resort and all,

37:05.140 --> 37:09.480
but isn't Eren controlling
the Founder through Zeke?

37:09.480 --> 37:13.690
Won't the rumbling stop
if we kill Zeke first?

37:14.500 --> 37:17.280
True. That might work!

37:17.280 --> 37:21.240
There's no definite proof,
but Hange thought it would.

37:21.240 --> 37:23.910
But if we don't know
Zeke's location either...

37:24.530 --> 37:31.000
We'll just have to find that shithead,
the Beast, in those bones.

37:39.330 --> 37:43.000
I'll take Zeke out.

37:45.100 --> 37:48.940
Help me do it.

37:50.480 --> 37:51.520
Captain...

37:53.110 --> 37:58.200
Of course. We killed many friends and
comrades to get this thing in the sky.

37:59.490 --> 38:03.410
We can't allow that slaughter
to have been for nothing.

38:04.570 --> 38:07.830
Everything is to stop the rumbling.

38:08.330 --> 38:09.960
I'll do whatever it takes.

38:11.290 --> 38:12.330
Jean...

38:12.960 --> 38:19.930
I shot Samuel and Daz
and sliced up other people I knew.

38:21.680 --> 38:24.220
I got called a traitor as I did so,

38:24.220 --> 38:28.400
all the while telling myself
it was to save the world.

38:30.810 --> 38:31.900
Tell me, Reiner.

38:32.560 --> 38:37.030
It was agonizing for you,
Bertholdt, and Annie too, wasn't it?

38:39.450 --> 38:43.030
I can't even make up
for the sins I committed anymore.

38:44.090 --> 38:49.290
Even if we save what remains of humanity,
I doubt I'll ever forgive myself.

38:57.260 --> 38:58.180
So...

38:58.760 --> 39:02.800
Well, let's at least save
what remains of humanity.

39:06.190 --> 39:08.560
You're right, Reiner.

39:09.100 --> 39:11.230
Even if we can't make up for it,

39:11.230 --> 39:14.350
we still gotta do what we can.

39:19.570 --> 39:23.950
That's right. We're the same, Reiner.

39:26.210 --> 39:29.330
I never had any right to judge you.

39:29.330 --> 39:33.830
I became a murderer to save others.

39:35.290 --> 39:36.380
You know...

39:37.720 --> 39:41.760
On the night of the raid on Liberio,
Eren said the same thing to me.

39:45.260 --> 39:50.020
I feel like I understand some
of what's going on in Eren's head.

39:50.600 --> 39:54.390
Could it be Eren wants us to stop him?

39:56.400 --> 39:57.860
What do you mean?

39:57.860 --> 40:01.740
I mean, it's just a thought
that occurred to me.

40:03.190 --> 40:06.290
Something's been bothering me
this whole time.

40:07.750 --> 40:12.910
Eren has the power to affect
all Titans and Eldians.

40:13.620 --> 40:18.510
And yet our ability to use our
Titan powers remains unchanged.

40:20.300 --> 40:24.010
You mean Eren is purposely
giving us free rein?

40:24.670 --> 40:27.430
Exactly. He's letting us act freely.

40:28.220 --> 40:32.520
As if to test how we
respond to what he's doing.

40:33.850 --> 40:38.030
Why? We might succeed
in stopping the rumbling.

40:38.610 --> 40:42.110
It has to be agonizing for him, too.

40:42.730 --> 40:46.910
Committing mass murder...
that's not a burden you can just bear.

40:47.370 --> 40:51.740
If it was me, I'd be desperate to leave
the Founder's power with someone else.

40:52.330 --> 40:55.700
And if that wasn't possible,
I'd want someone...

40:58.240 --> 40:59.420
to end it.

41:00.500 --> 41:01.460
What?

41:08.510 --> 41:09.810
Again?!

41:09.810 --> 41:10.930
This is...

41:14.350 --> 41:17.440
What, was he listening in?

41:18.070 --> 41:20.190
Eren! Please hear me out!

41:20.520 --> 41:22.150
This is already enough!

41:22.150 --> 41:27.740
I'm sure no one will attack the
island for hundreds of years!

41:27.740 --> 41:31.580
The terror and destruction
have been just that extreme!

41:31.580 --> 41:35.700
If you stop now, we can end all this
by agreeing to a non-aggression treaty!

41:35.700 --> 41:38.290
You don't have to kill any more people!

41:38.290 --> 41:40.540
The island will be okay now!

41:44.790 --> 41:46.890
It was all our fault!

41:46.890 --> 41:49.850
We were the ones who drove you this far!

41:51.180 --> 41:52.350
Eren...

41:52.350 --> 41:53.600
Eren!

41:53.600 --> 41:55.930
We'll figure out the rest!

41:56.440 --> 42:00.690
You don't have to keep
committing genocide for our sake!

42:01.150 --> 42:02.940
That's right.

42:02.940 --> 42:03.810
Eren!

42:04.520 --> 42:07.160
I hated you after what happened to Sasha,

42:07.160 --> 42:09.950
but in truth, you were
hurting too, weren't you?!

42:10.370 --> 42:13.780
And yet, I didn't even try to see things
from your perspective at all!

42:18.790 --> 42:19.790
Eren...

42:20.460 --> 42:24.750
I... I want to shoulder your sins with you.

42:24.750 --> 42:28.220
The sins you've committed...
We're guilty of them, too.

42:28.970 --> 42:32.800
So please, don't push us away anymore.

42:33.930 --> 42:37.810
Please, Eren, come back to us!

42:39.690 --> 42:41.270
You heard 'em, Eren.

42:41.810 --> 42:45.020
Do it now, and I'll let you off
with just a swift kick in the ass.

42:46.200 --> 42:49.450
Well? Ain't it about time
you said something?

42:54.860 --> 42:55.950
Eren?!

42:56.750 --> 42:58.960
The rumbling will not stop.

43:00.040 --> 43:05.170
Nor will I leave Paradis Island's
future to chance.

43:06.340 --> 43:08.470
I will keep moving forward.

43:12.260 --> 43:13.320
Look.

43:23.190 --> 43:24.270
Eren!

43:27.950 --> 43:30.530
Huh?! Ain't that... a kid?!

43:30.530 --> 43:32.820
Yeah, but that's Eren!

43:40.940 --> 43:41.830
Eren!

43:41.830 --> 43:44.160
Why refuse, Eren?

43:44.160 --> 43:46.470
You think you can't rely on us?

43:47.300 --> 43:51.130
Why did you leave us able
to use our Titan powers?

43:51.130 --> 43:53.220
We can talk for as long
as we want here, right?

43:53.550 --> 43:54.920
Talk to us!

43:54.920 --> 43:56.890
We've always been together!

43:56.890 --> 43:59.230
Please don't go any farther away!

43:59.640 --> 44:00.980
Eren!

44:01.480 --> 44:06.990
In order to obtain freedom,
I will take freedom from the world.

44:07.650 --> 44:11.610
But I will not take
anything from any of you.

44:12.740 --> 44:14.610
You all have freedom.

44:18.080 --> 44:21.620
You are free to protect the world's freedom.

44:23.160 --> 44:26.040
And I am free to keep moving forward.

44:27.130 --> 44:32.760
As long as we each hold unbending
convictions, a clash is inevitable.

44:35.130 --> 44:37.970
There is but one thing for us to do.

44:39.390 --> 44:40.650
Fight.

44:43.350 --> 44:45.020
But...

44:45.810 --> 44:47.320
Then why...

44:47.990 --> 44:50.430
Why did you call us here?

44:51.440 --> 44:55.530
To discuss the fact that there's
no need to have a discussion.

44:57.990 --> 45:00.410
If you wish to stop me,

45:00.410 --> 45:02.950
make me draw my last breath.

45:04.240 --> 45:06.420
You have freedom.

45:12.500 --> 45:13.420
What was that?

45:13.420 --> 45:14.250
Is everyone okay?

45:16.760 --> 45:20.390
It looks like I was right.

45:21.030 --> 45:23.760
So there's really no way to work this out?

45:27.690 --> 45:30.230
Looks like we aren't gonna
solve this by talking.

45:31.020 --> 45:32.020
What now...

45:33.370 --> 45:34.520
Commander?

45:45.780 --> 45:47.790
Where are we going now?

45:48.090 --> 45:51.460
We'll spend the next several days
making the voyage to Hizuru.

45:51.460 --> 45:56.040
I have faith that Lady Mikasa's group
will hold off the rumbling.

45:56.430 --> 46:01.600
However, I expect that Hizuru is already
in a state of collapse as a nation.

46:02.850 --> 46:06.310
Sounds like there'll be nothing
to eat but fish for a while.

46:06.930 --> 46:10.060
Hizuru's fish dishes are splendid.

46:10.610 --> 46:12.150
Good.

46:12.150 --> 46:14.810
Oh, guess there'll be birds to eat, too.

46:19.180 --> 46:22.450
I am the one who brought
Zeke and Eren together.

46:24.450 --> 46:26.580
I imagine there's nothing I can do to atone

46:26.580 --> 46:29.960
for the sin of bringing
about this mass slaughter.

46:33.040 --> 46:36.260
Then, if you could go back
and redo everything,

46:36.260 --> 46:40.720
would you refrain from getting involved
with Eldians and watch Paradis die?

46:42.890 --> 46:45.550
Time will not turn back.

46:46.220 --> 46:50.020
But my sense of regret will never end.

46:50.980 --> 46:56.950
I cannot say that I did everything in my
power to find a path for Eldian survival.

46:57.990 --> 47:03.740
I treated my clan's interests and my
family's honor as my greatest duties.

47:10.620 --> 47:15.210
Why must we experience loss
before we can realize...

47:17.510 --> 47:22.260
how to respect and value others
without putting ourselves first?

47:25.530 --> 47:29.380
But now... it's too late.

47:33.350 --> 47:36.860
Annie, I... had a dream.

47:37.530 --> 47:40.240
A dream? Was it from Galliard?

47:40.700 --> 47:44.150
It was a dream from Zeke...
No, they were memories.

47:44.150 --> 47:48.120
If I recall, the Female Titan can
manifest the abilities of other Titans

47:48.120 --> 47:50.500
by taking in a part of those Titans, right?

47:50.500 --> 47:54.290
Yeah. Since the Female is
particularly suited to manifesting,

47:54.290 --> 47:55.890
I had to swallow all sorts of stuff.

47:55.890 --> 47:57.160
But why does that matter?

47:57.160 --> 47:58.760
It's like we thought! So, then—

47:58.760 --> 48:00.760
There might be something we can do!

48:00.760 --> 48:02.130
But no... Wait, do you think—

48:02.130 --> 48:03.510
Oh, be quiet already!

48:03.510 --> 48:05.380
Go carry some coal or something!

48:09.100 --> 48:12.020
Did you say you saw memories from Zeke?

48:12.390 --> 48:17.150
Yes. I was turned into a Titan
using Zeke's spinal fluid.

48:17.150 --> 48:21.030
It seems he's manifesting characteristics
of the Beast Titan because of that.

48:21.530 --> 48:24.400
I see. Go on.

48:24.940 --> 48:27.160
The memory I see most often is...

48:27.870 --> 48:30.330
a memory of flying above the clouds.

48:30.980 --> 48:34.310
And that's not all. I can do it, too.

48:35.220 --> 48:37.090
That's how it feels to me.

48:48.980 --> 48:51.060
That's Fort Salta...

48:51.060 --> 48:53.100
Are there really airships there?

48:53.100 --> 48:58.080
Beats me. We won't know
until we get up there.

48:58.080 --> 49:01.730
Do you really think you can
escape by stealing an airship?

49:01.730 --> 49:04.040
You Eldians?

49:07.080 --> 49:09.660
Watch your mouth, Marleyan.

49:10.240 --> 49:14.160
It's thanks to us that you haven't
been squished under a Titan's foot.

49:14.160 --> 49:18.550
If the airship idea doesn't work,
your family will die in the rumbling.

49:19.050 --> 49:21.920
If you betray us, you'll die from my bullet.

49:22.300 --> 49:25.550
This is the only way for all of you to live.

49:25.880 --> 49:30.810
It doesn't matter if the chance is slim.
We're gonna survive.

49:35.560 --> 49:37.900
It's okay, Mrs. Braun.

49:37.900 --> 49:39.640
Those two are strong.

49:39.640 --> 49:41.980
I'm sure they're with Colt and Reiner—

49:41.980 --> 49:44.610
Our girl is on the devils' island!

49:44.610 --> 49:47.030
How could she survive there?

49:48.080 --> 49:50.780
If only she'd never tried
to become a Warrior,

49:50.780 --> 49:53.080
we could've been together in the end...

49:56.750 --> 49:58.210
Reiner...

49:59.460 --> 50:02.710
Mr. Finger, throw that
armband out the window.

50:03.120 --> 50:09.160
This armband is something my daughter
earned by sacrificing everything to help me.

50:10.180 --> 50:11.220
Ugh...

50:12.140 --> 50:13.220
Hey! Look there!

50:13.970 --> 50:16.980
Oh, no! The airships!

50:17.480 --> 50:19.860
Hurry! We can make it
if there's even one left!

50:19.860 --> 50:20.730
I know!

50:28.870 --> 50:31.870
Hey, what's that fog?

50:33.320 --> 50:35.120
It's the rumbling.

50:35.830 --> 50:38.630
It's finally caught up to us...

50:49.860 --> 50:52.640
We're screwed! There isn't a single one left!

50:55.140 --> 50:59.020
No... Not after we made it this far...

50:59.020 --> 51:00.440
Why...

51:00.440 --> 51:01.900
It's all over.

51:04.520 --> 51:05.650
Hold on...

51:06.310 --> 51:10.160
Those airships...
are heading toward the Titans!

51:10.160 --> 51:11.780
What does that mean?

51:11.780 --> 51:13.240
It's a bombing run!

51:13.240 --> 51:16.160
They're gonna blow the Titans away
from the safety of the sky!

51:16.160 --> 51:19.670
They intend to stake the fate
of all humanity on this!

51:22.420 --> 51:24.120
A bombing run?!

51:24.790 --> 51:26.420
Are we gonna be saved?

51:27.510 --> 51:32.550
Attention, all airship units and
every soldier in this fortress.

51:33.490 --> 51:37.440
This fortress will be
the last bastion left to humanity.

51:39.440 --> 51:43.940
The pressure weighing down
on your shoulders is immeasurable.

51:43.940 --> 51:46.950
But no matter the result,

51:46.950 --> 51:49.950
the responsibility does not
lie solely with you.

51:52.490 --> 51:53.950
The responsibility for this

51:54.530 --> 51:57.460
lies with all of us adults.

51:58.000 --> 51:59.710
We took advantage of hate...

51:59.710 --> 52:02.000
instilled and fostered it...

52:02.000 --> 52:04.710
believing it would bring us salvation.

52:04.710 --> 52:07.630
All the problems arising from our faults

52:07.630 --> 52:10.300
we dumped onto the "island of devils."

52:11.220 --> 52:12.970
As a result,

52:12.970 --> 52:15.220
that monster was born,

52:15.220 --> 52:18.980
and now it's marching our hatred
right back toward us.

52:22.430 --> 52:24.850
If, by some miracle,

52:24.850 --> 52:27.280
we manage to have a future again,

52:27.860 --> 52:33.610
I vow to never repeat the same mistake.

53:03.100 --> 53:04.140
Ms. Braun?

53:04.140 --> 53:05.310
Karina?!

53:05.310 --> 53:11.360
This whole time... I treated my boy...
as a tool for revenge...

53:11.980 --> 53:16.910
I've still never done...
a single motherly thing for him...

53:18.910 --> 53:20.120
I did the same thing...

53:21.080 --> 53:23.660
I hope you will all make the same vow.

53:24.830 --> 53:27.710
To break away from our era of mutual hate...

53:28.630 --> 53:31.420
The airship units are in formation!

53:31.420 --> 53:34.630
They'll begin the bombardment
upon reaching the target altitude!

53:35.550 --> 53:38.600
To create a new world where
people take care of each other...

53:39.760 --> 53:44.470
Here and now, we say farewell
to our monster!

53:53.150 --> 53:54.770
The Attack Titan is taking action!

53:55.190 --> 53:57.530
Begin the bombardment!

53:58.160 --> 53:59.740
Bombs away!

54:20.260 --> 54:23.260
They're so high up that the bombs keep missing!

54:23.260 --> 54:24.760
Have them continue!

54:24.760 --> 54:27.020
Put everything into this attack!

55:25.740 --> 55:27.290
The airship units...

55:28.370 --> 55:31.750
have been wiped out.

55:37.180 --> 55:38.680
I am sorry.

55:41.460 --> 55:44.130
All you innocent children... We failed you.

55:44.130 --> 55:46.130
Hey... Mommy...

55:47.060 --> 55:49.140
The Titans are coming this way.

55:50.230 --> 55:51.690
I'm scared...

55:51.690 --> 55:53.140
I'm so sorry.

55:56.820 --> 56:01.400
I'm certain Annie and Reiner
are alive on Paradis Island.

56:02.700 --> 56:03.740
Yes...

56:15.160 --> 56:16.410
Look.

56:18.920 --> 56:20.220
What is that?

56:27.810 --> 56:30.430
Dammit! We're running on fumes!

56:38.440 --> 56:39.320
I see him!

56:39.320 --> 56:41.110
Get ready to jump!

56:41.110 --> 56:43.190
Onyankopon, you get over here, too!

56:43.190 --> 56:46.190
Not yet! I'll keep going
till we're over the Founder!

56:47.700 --> 56:50.200
Afterwards, I'll make an emergency landing!

56:50.200 --> 56:53.750
So make sure you land
on the Founding Titan! Got that?

56:53.750 --> 56:55.250
Onyankopon!

57:01.760 --> 57:02.840
The bastard's down there.

57:03.840 --> 57:05.960
That damned Beast!

57:06.590 --> 57:08.350
That saves us the trouble of finding him!

57:08.930 --> 57:11.100
Target the Beast Titan!

57:11.470 --> 57:14.100
Put all your power into taking him out!

57:14.680 --> 57:16.600
Let's stop the rumbling!

57:27.290 --> 57:28.040
Now!

57:33.740 --> 57:35.120
Eren!

58:02.550 --> 58:04.860
Damn it! I can't land!

58:24.000 --> 58:25.040
Reiner!

58:49.950 --> 58:51.870
The Armored Titan...

58:52.280 --> 58:54.410
and even the Cart Titan?!

58:54.410 --> 58:57.130
That's ODM gear...

58:57.130 --> 59:00.920
Could it be?! Paradis Island
came to stop the rumbling?!

59:03.040 --> 59:04.460
Reiner!

59:09.220 --> 59:10.430
Eren.

59:11.090 --> 59:13.680
I have another question to ask you,

59:14.120 --> 59:17.150
once we drag you out of there.

59:18.130 --> 59:20.940
"In what way are you free?"

59:25.600 --> 59:27.780
CHAPTER 3

59:27.780 --> 59:35.620
CHAPTER 3
THE BATTLE OF HEAVEN AND EARTH

01:00:00.770 --> 01:00:02.640
I guess killing some empty husk

01:00:03.060 --> 01:00:04.690
isn't gonna do anything.

01:00:05.100 --> 01:00:06.020
As I feared...

01:00:06.390 --> 01:00:10.650
Zeke's using the same method as
the War Hammer Titan to hide himself.

01:00:10.650 --> 01:00:16.650
You mean we have to find one tiny body
in this huge mass of bones?!

01:00:16.650 --> 01:00:18.790
There ain't no way!

01:00:18.790 --> 01:00:21.540
We gotta face up to reality!

01:00:21.540 --> 01:00:22.460
Armin!

01:00:22.460 --> 01:00:23.500
I know!

01:00:26.370 --> 01:00:28.260
In one minute, I'm blasting this area away.

01:00:28.590 --> 01:00:31.420
Work with the Cart Titan to get clear!

01:00:33.420 --> 01:00:34.600
Armin...

01:00:35.470 --> 01:00:39.640
Eren knows this attack could be coming.
I can't imagine this'll kill him!

01:00:40.160 --> 01:00:46.760
But if I blow these bones apart,
we might figure out where Eren or Zeke is!

01:00:48.940 --> 01:00:50.690
Be careful, Armin!

01:00:50.690 --> 01:00:55.780
If you get into trouble,
ignore us and just go full blast!

01:01:01.160 --> 01:01:05.870
Those who can't abandon anything
can't change anything.

01:01:06.450 --> 01:01:07.840
I know that.

01:01:07.840 --> 01:01:10.590
If I don't let go, nothing will change.

01:01:11.760 --> 01:01:14.380
I can't cling to my comfortable hopes.

01:01:15.880 --> 01:01:19.140
I have to deal with Eren.

01:01:21.890 --> 01:01:22.810
Armin!

01:01:35.040 --> 01:01:35.940
Armin!

01:01:54.090 --> 01:01:57.310
On three! One, two, three!

01:01:58.140 --> 01:01:59.890
He's not moving.

01:01:59.890 --> 01:02:01.220
He's breathing.

01:02:02.260 --> 01:02:03.810
It appears he hit his head.

01:02:04.430 --> 01:02:07.770
Do you think he came here
from Paradis Island, too?

01:02:07.770 --> 01:02:09.820
Hey! Can you hear me?

01:02:10.320 --> 01:02:12.320
Do you know Annie Leonhart?

01:02:12.730 --> 01:02:14.690
She's my daughter!

01:02:15.070 --> 01:02:17.990
Hey! Sir! Do you hear me?!

01:02:20.330 --> 01:02:21.950
Here they come! Reiner!

01:02:43.510 --> 01:02:45.260
What the hell are these guys?

01:02:51.020 --> 01:02:54.410
They don't look like Pure Titans.
That's for sure.

01:02:55.270 --> 01:02:58.070
What do we do?
We'll run out of Thunder Spears!

01:02:58.070 --> 01:03:00.410
More importantly, is Armin alive?

01:03:00.840 --> 01:03:04.350
The slightest injury,
and he would've transformed.

01:03:04.740 --> 01:03:07.920
Which means he was captured
without a scratch.

01:03:08.670 --> 01:03:12.210
But he was whisked off towards Eren's ass,

01:03:12.630 --> 01:03:15.420
with countless Titans blocking our path.

01:03:15.750 --> 01:03:20.090
Even in perfect condition,
I wouldn't choose to leap into that mess.

01:03:20.410 --> 01:03:22.630
So keep cool.

01:03:23.930 --> 01:03:26.220
Mikasa, don't charge off.

01:03:26.220 --> 01:03:30.060
I'll act as bait and draw
the bulk of them away first.

01:03:30.060 --> 01:03:32.310
That won't work, Captain.

01:03:32.730 --> 01:03:35.810
I've figured out what we're
dealing with. They're...

01:03:36.350 --> 01:03:38.540
...the past generations
of the Nine Titans.

01:03:39.070 --> 01:03:42.320
Who knows if their minds
are still in there, though.

01:03:42.740 --> 01:03:48.330
I would bet the Founding Titan's power
can resurrect an unlimited number of them...

01:03:48.970 --> 01:03:53.460
These past Titan soldiers created only to fight.

01:03:53.960 --> 01:03:56.670
We're no match for something like that.

01:03:56.670 --> 01:03:57.470
Exactly.

01:03:57.760 --> 01:04:00.760
So we can't afford to be
so easygoing with this.

01:04:00.760 --> 01:04:04.340
I'm not even friends with Eren, so...

01:04:04.340 --> 01:04:05.200
What?!

01:04:05.630 --> 01:04:06.720
Hey! You're not gonna...

01:04:06.720 --> 01:04:07.770
Pieck!

01:04:08.140 --> 01:04:09.390
Aw, hell.

01:04:24.240 --> 01:04:27.370
No matter how you look at it,
this is the first place to strike!

01:04:27.370 --> 01:04:29.430
I've only ever had one aim here!

01:04:32.540 --> 01:04:33.540
Wait!

01:04:34.330 --> 01:04:36.540
Begone, nightmare!

01:04:52.680 --> 01:04:53.480
Pieck!

01:04:58.530 --> 01:04:59.530
Galliard?!

01:04:59.990 --> 01:05:01.320
Over here, Reiner!

01:05:01.940 --> 01:05:03.860
Keep him still!

01:05:12.540 --> 01:05:13.840
Captain!

01:05:15.200 --> 01:05:18.340
Hurry. We're getting Armin back.

01:05:18.340 --> 01:05:20.420
That's our only path through this.

01:05:20.420 --> 01:05:24.010
Otherwise, we'll all die here for nothing!

01:05:25.340 --> 01:05:29.390
Paradis forces have engaged the Attack Titan,

01:05:29.390 --> 01:05:33.430
but its path and speed remain
unchanged. It's headed this way!

01:05:34.520 --> 01:05:36.810
We can't just sit back and do nothing.

01:05:37.220 --> 01:05:39.900
All units, meet the enemy with cannon fire!

01:05:39.900 --> 01:05:40.650
Yes, sir!

01:05:40.650 --> 01:05:44.820
But, sir! The majority of our personnel
were sent with the airships.

01:05:44.820 --> 01:05:49.120
We only have enough remaining
to operate three cannons at best...

01:05:49.120 --> 01:05:53.040
Is that any reason for us
to sit back and do nothing?

01:05:54.580 --> 01:05:59.920
Even now, those brave individuals are fighting
desperately on the enemy's massive back.

01:06:00.250 --> 01:06:03.590
Just what is it that you think
they're fighting for?

01:06:03.590 --> 01:06:05.340
Come on, Reiner!

01:06:27.740 --> 01:06:28.710
Hurry!

01:06:36.620 --> 01:06:37.630
Mikasa!

01:06:49.350 --> 01:06:50.940
I was naive.

01:06:52.510 --> 01:06:53.960
I'm gonna pass out...

01:06:55.520 --> 01:06:58.560
You're just going to suffocate me?

01:06:59.270 --> 01:07:02.830
Is that it, Eren?

01:07:04.060 --> 01:07:07.180
No, this isn't him.

01:07:07.180 --> 01:07:08.990
It's her, the Founder Ymir.

01:07:09.620 --> 01:07:14.370
If Eren only intends to keep
moving forward, as he put it,

01:07:14.800 --> 01:07:18.380
then this resistance is
the Founder Ymir's will.

01:07:18.780 --> 01:07:24.920
Which means Ymir wants
to slaughter humanity, too.

01:07:26.260 --> 01:07:29.340
The Founder Ymir is invincible.

01:07:30.080 --> 01:07:32.140
There's nothing I can do.

01:07:33.470 --> 01:07:40.220
Is this... where it all... ends?

01:07:58.470 --> 01:07:59.750
Bertholdt...

01:08:09.260 --> 01:08:12.760
Reiner!

01:08:25.350 --> 01:08:27.570
Are you kidding me?

01:09:00.520 --> 01:09:02.770
Wake up, Conny! Captain!

01:09:10.070 --> 01:09:13.990
Sorry. Looks like my ODM gear is damaged.

01:09:13.990 --> 01:09:15.320
Mine, too.

01:09:15.320 --> 01:09:19.700
My right handle's busted. I can't pull us up.

01:09:20.250 --> 01:09:23.870
Jean, let go! I can transform one more time!

01:09:24.580 --> 01:09:29.710
And then what? Only to get trampled
in the rumbling, armor and all?

01:09:29.710 --> 01:09:34.380
For being armored,
your Titan sure gets smashed up a lot.

01:09:35.710 --> 01:09:38.680
You think we can still win?

01:09:39.180 --> 01:09:40.660
Nope.

01:09:40.660 --> 01:09:44.640
But let's at least keep fighting
all the way to the end.

01:09:45.110 --> 01:09:49.650
We're Scout Regiment.
Scouts don't know when to quit.

01:09:53.010 --> 01:09:54.010
Jean...

01:10:03.770 --> 01:10:04.990
Conny!

01:10:13.960 --> 01:10:14.960
Captain!

01:10:34.320 --> 01:10:35.610
Come at me!

01:10:36.150 --> 01:10:37.780
I'm strong!

01:10:37.780 --> 01:10:38.620
So...

01:10:39.200 --> 01:10:40.990
No matter how many times you attack—

01:10:40.990 --> 01:10:42.410
Mikasa, you're kinda in the way!

01:10:42.410 --> 01:10:43.370
What?

01:10:44.410 --> 01:10:45.490
Grab on!

01:11:08.980 --> 01:11:14.060
Listen, I didn't think
he'd really be able to fly, either...

01:11:14.730 --> 01:11:19.240
But then he actually did it,
so what choice did I have but to come?

01:11:22.370 --> 01:11:25.240
Still, I'm glad I did.

01:11:27.750 --> 01:11:28.960
A bird...

01:11:29.340 --> 01:11:31.000
It's got people riding on it!

01:11:32.500 --> 01:11:34.960
Gabi, why did you come here too?

01:11:34.960 --> 01:11:37.500
Because you left us behind, Reiner!

01:11:37.970 --> 01:11:39.640
I can fight too, you know!

01:11:39.640 --> 01:11:40.640
Annie!

01:11:42.300 --> 01:11:44.640
The Azumabito ship sank.

01:11:46.510 --> 01:11:49.100
It couldn't withstand
Falco's Titan transformation.

01:11:50.400 --> 01:11:53.150
Even though we had no
definite proof he could fly,

01:11:53.150 --> 01:11:55.730
Kiyomi agreed to try it.

01:11:56.480 --> 01:12:01.410
So we have to repay her faith
by stopping the rumbling!

01:12:02.160 --> 01:12:03.410
Gabi...

01:12:03.820 --> 01:12:07.200
So where's Arm—I mean, Pieck?

01:12:07.200 --> 01:12:09.790
Armin was captured, and his life is in danger.

01:12:10.790 --> 01:12:13.540
The Titan that took him
should be back by the tailbone.

01:12:14.040 --> 01:12:16.040
Annie, we need your help.

01:12:16.860 --> 01:12:20.160
Your childhood friends are always
getting captured, aren't they?

01:12:20.970 --> 01:12:22.930
We'll get him back. Count on it.

01:12:23.300 --> 01:12:24.590
What about Pieck?

01:12:24.590 --> 01:12:26.300
She's by the skull.

01:12:26.300 --> 01:12:28.230
She tried to blow up the nape.

01:12:28.230 --> 01:12:30.350
But the War Hammer Titan
is blocking her.

01:12:30.350 --> 01:12:31.520
Blow it up?!

01:12:31.520 --> 01:12:33.200
We'll launch simultaneous operations.

01:12:33.810 --> 01:12:35.060
Captain!

01:12:36.390 --> 01:12:38.820
One group rescues Armin.

01:12:38.820 --> 01:12:41.530
We need the Colossal's explosion.

01:12:42.110 --> 01:12:45.570
The other group goes after Eren
and attacks the nape.

01:12:45.950 --> 01:12:48.460
We'll split into two teams
and strike simultaneously.

01:12:49.500 --> 01:12:53.620
We no longer have the luxury
of worrying about Eren.

01:12:54.290 --> 01:12:58.340
No, we never had it to begin with.

01:12:59.410 --> 01:13:00.800
Captain...

01:13:01.340 --> 01:13:02.220
But—

01:13:02.220 --> 01:13:03.590
But what?

01:13:03.590 --> 01:13:07.340
Falco being able to fly was a miracle.
Without that, we'd already be dead!

01:13:09.600 --> 01:13:12.850
Yeah, and never have
accomplished anything...

01:13:13.230 --> 01:13:14.230
Jean...

01:13:14.230 --> 01:13:18.570
I had a long list of shit
to tell that idiot off about...

01:13:18.900 --> 01:13:19.740
Fuck!

01:13:20.070 --> 01:13:22.900
I don't wanna give up on Eren, either!

01:13:22.900 --> 01:13:26.990
But the captain can't
fight anymore because of me,

01:13:27.310 --> 01:13:29.950
and even if he could,
we're up against the Founding Titan!

01:13:29.950 --> 01:13:33.000
How can we win if we're still holding back?

01:13:38.710 --> 01:13:40.010
Mikasa...

01:13:40.970 --> 01:13:42.060
let's...

01:13:43.060 --> 01:13:44.210
Let's...

01:13:44.850 --> 01:13:46.010
kill Eren.

01:13:48.390 --> 01:13:49.350
Mikasa.

01:13:49.720 --> 01:13:50.720
Mikasa.

01:13:51.020 --> 01:13:52.020
Mikasa!

01:13:52.020 --> 01:13:55.020
You just concentrate on rescuing Armin.

01:13:58.150 --> 01:14:01.030
You don't have to think about anything else.

01:14:03.070 --> 01:14:04.030
Okay.

01:14:17.490 --> 01:14:20.130
They're heading for the Attack Titan again!

01:14:20.550 --> 01:14:21.960
We can't let up, either!

01:14:21.960 --> 01:14:24.800
Even if it's just one or two cannons,
it's better than nothing!

01:14:28.260 --> 01:14:29.970
Refugees?

01:14:29.970 --> 01:14:31.640
Wait. Maybe not.

01:14:32.430 --> 01:14:35.470
Look at the fading on their left sleeves...

01:14:36.470 --> 01:14:38.270
You're Eldians, aren't you?!

01:14:39.520 --> 01:14:40.690
Hey!

01:14:40.690 --> 01:14:42.020
Hold on!

01:14:42.650 --> 01:14:45.400
We only came to seek
treatment for our injured!

01:14:45.400 --> 01:14:47.320
We don't have time to deal with this!

01:14:47.320 --> 01:14:49.160
What's your real objective?

01:14:49.660 --> 01:14:53.660
See, Mr. Leonhart? I told you.
We can't expect help from Marleyans!

01:14:53.930 --> 01:14:58.040
We have them beat in numbers.
And probably in live combat experience, too!

01:14:58.040 --> 01:15:02.040
The Marleyans always sent us
to the front lines, after all.

01:15:04.540 --> 01:15:06.110
Put down your guns, Eldians!

01:15:07.770 --> 01:15:08.550
Stop!

01:15:08.550 --> 01:15:10.660
They said to put down your guns!

01:15:11.810 --> 01:15:12.930
Conductor?

01:15:13.300 --> 01:15:14.930
When did you...?

01:15:27.060 --> 01:15:28.450
Secretary Müller!

01:15:42.460 --> 01:15:43.460
What was that?

01:15:43.460 --> 01:15:45.960
People are still trying to kill each other?!

01:15:46.960 --> 01:15:49.340
Falco! Watch out for projectiles!

01:15:55.970 --> 01:15:56.970
Incoming!

01:16:13.700 --> 01:16:14.990
Jean! Reiner!

01:16:14.990 --> 01:16:16.200
Don't get killed!

01:16:19.230 --> 01:16:21.840
Don't you guys die, either.

01:16:22.580 --> 01:16:26.210
I'll draw the War Hammer Titans' attention!

01:16:27.790 --> 01:16:31.340
Pieck, find some way to hold out.

01:16:52.950 --> 01:16:54.360
Now, Jean!

01:17:00.910 --> 01:17:02.720
Just hang on, Reiner!

01:17:04.210 --> 01:17:05.710
Until I can activate that detonator!

01:17:09.550 --> 01:17:12.550
Of course there'd be even
more Titans thrown at us.

01:17:17.880 --> 01:17:20.890
I wish I could move omni-directionally, too!

01:17:27.430 --> 01:17:29.650
Dammit! I can't get close!

01:17:35.150 --> 01:17:35.900
Pieck!

01:17:35.900 --> 01:17:36.820
Don't! Get outta there!

01:17:41.660 --> 01:17:46.750
Jean, if you think I'm a Titan for odd jobs
and not cut out for combat,

01:17:47.410 --> 01:17:49.090
you're dead wrong!

01:17:50.670 --> 01:17:54.420
With the Cart's endurance,
as long as I'm not taken out,

01:17:54.420 --> 01:17:56.710
I can keep going until I've won!

01:17:58.470 --> 01:18:00.220
Even if it takes hundreds of transformations!

01:18:02.220 --> 01:18:05.770
So, Jean, don't worry about me.
Get to the detonator!

01:18:16.100 --> 01:18:21.990
Though, a hundred victories won't
do much against a million enemies.

01:18:31.630 --> 01:18:35.250
How dare they make Bertholdt into a puppet?

01:18:36.940 --> 01:18:37.800
There it is!

01:18:38.350 --> 01:18:41.350
That one! The... pig one, or whatever it is!

01:18:41.350 --> 01:18:42.180
Which one?

01:18:42.180 --> 01:18:44.680
That one! The... thingy. Over there!

01:18:44.680 --> 01:18:45.560
Where?

01:18:45.560 --> 01:18:47.970
Which type of the Nine Titans is it?

01:18:47.970 --> 01:18:51.820
Might be Cart... or Beast... or maybe Jaw.

01:18:51.820 --> 01:18:53.070
What do I do with that?

01:18:53.070 --> 01:18:55.190
Mikasa, give me a serious description!

01:18:55.190 --> 01:18:56.070
I did!

01:18:56.070 --> 01:18:58.950
There! The one Titan that just ran!

01:18:59.620 --> 01:19:00.660
That?

01:19:00.660 --> 01:19:01.950
Isn't that an okapi?

01:19:01.950 --> 01:19:03.330
What the hell is an okapi?

01:19:03.330 --> 01:19:04.450
Go, Falco!

01:19:04.450 --> 01:19:08.080
We'll corner that okapi, or whatever it is,
at the tailbone and get Armin back!

01:19:14.040 --> 01:19:17.130
I can provide support with this rifle.

01:19:17.130 --> 01:19:19.850
It'll take more than that
to do in these Titans.

01:19:21.260 --> 01:19:23.220
Where's Zeke?

01:19:23.220 --> 01:19:24.850
Where is he?

01:19:26.350 --> 01:19:30.310
Even if I find him, in my condition,
I'll only be in the way...

01:19:30.310 --> 01:19:31.610
Dammit!

01:19:34.190 --> 01:19:38.510
I've never failed to carry out
one of his orders. Not once.

01:19:39.350 --> 01:19:43.810
Why has his final order
caused me so many problems?

01:19:46.810 --> 01:19:51.370
Maybe our jobs were over at that point.

01:19:52.810 --> 01:19:57.840
If all we had to do was deliver
the brats to the sea, then...

01:19:59.720 --> 01:20:03.970
Tell me, did the lives you gave in sacrifice

01:20:04.300 --> 01:20:07.240
exist to crush others' lives underfoot?

01:20:09.250 --> 01:20:10.440
No.

01:20:11.810 --> 01:20:14.900
The world without Titans we dreamed of

01:20:14.900 --> 01:20:18.780
was supposed to be an astoundingly
joyful place. An ideal world.

01:20:20.000 --> 01:20:24.240
Otherwise, it wouldn't be worth
the hearts they gave.

01:20:25.490 --> 01:20:32.620
Erwin, I have no regrets about
my decision not to choose you...

01:20:35.330 --> 01:20:40.260
to entrust the future to someone
with the same look in his eyes you all had.

01:20:48.800 --> 01:20:50.800
Conny! It went your way!

01:20:55.440 --> 01:20:57.290
Get back here!

01:21:01.240 --> 01:21:02.240
No!

01:21:02.240 --> 01:21:03.610
Now it can run back toward the skull!

01:21:03.610 --> 01:21:04.860
Annie!

01:21:18.550 --> 01:21:20.220
Stop running, okapi!

01:21:47.900 --> 01:21:49.080
Annie!

01:21:53.910 --> 01:21:57.030
We have to stay together,
or we'll be too easy to kill!

01:21:59.550 --> 01:22:01.550
The okapi is headed toward Bertholdt!

01:22:01.920 --> 01:22:02.800
Not good.

01:22:04.050 --> 01:22:04.800
Behind us!

01:22:21.070 --> 01:22:22.230
Come on, move!

01:22:23.150 --> 01:22:26.150
You're my body! Why won't you move?

01:22:26.830 --> 01:22:28.990
I'm begging you! Move!

01:22:28.990 --> 01:22:30.790
Everyone's going to die!

01:22:31.700 --> 01:22:32.700
Reiner...

01:22:33.330 --> 01:22:34.330
Pieck...

01:22:34.830 --> 01:22:35.950
Jean...

01:22:36.160 --> 01:22:37.580
Conny...

01:22:37.790 --> 01:22:39.210
Mikasa...

01:22:39.800 --> 01:22:40.800
Annie...

01:22:42.210 --> 01:22:44.550
They're all gonna die!

01:22:44.550 --> 01:22:45.840
Get up, you human garbage!

01:22:46.130 --> 01:22:47.340
Piece of shit!

01:22:47.340 --> 01:22:49.560
Waste of space!

01:22:52.500 --> 01:22:54.600
I hate you!

01:22:55.580 --> 01:22:59.980
Through everything, you've
just continued to betray me!

01:23:00.470 --> 01:23:03.860
The second life we were given!
The hopes pinned on us! Our responsibilities!

01:23:03.860 --> 01:23:08.620
All that, and you haven't even
begun to repay any of it!

01:23:08.920 --> 01:23:12.030
So what the hell are you
doing lying here dead?

01:23:12.030 --> 01:23:13.580
Move!

01:23:13.580 --> 01:23:16.450
Get your ass up!

01:25:09.150 --> 01:25:10.400
Sand...

01:25:11.950 --> 01:25:13.080
Think.

01:25:13.730 --> 01:25:15.610
If I were really dead,

01:25:15.610 --> 01:25:20.250
how could I think in a state
where my brain is deprived of oxygen?

01:25:22.970 --> 01:25:27.750
This isn't a dream, or a hallucination,
or the afterlife.

01:25:29.440 --> 01:25:31.090
This is the Paths.

01:25:32.570 --> 01:25:33.760
This is...

01:25:34.720 --> 01:25:35.760
reality!

01:25:40.670 --> 01:25:46.520
I should be inside a Titan's mouth.
So how is it I know what's happening to them?

01:25:47.600 --> 01:25:51.820
Is it because Eldians are all
connected through the Paths?

01:25:52.780 --> 01:25:56.990
If that's true, there might be
something I can accomplish here.

01:25:58.050 --> 01:26:00.290
That's it. Think.

01:26:01.540 --> 01:26:02.290
Think!

01:26:19.980 --> 01:26:22.310
Hello, Zeke.

01:26:30.670 --> 01:26:33.950
Hello, Eren's friend.

01:26:34.880 --> 01:26:37.500
You were consumed by Ymir, too?

01:26:41.830 --> 01:26:43.990
CHAPTER 4

01:26:43.990 --> 01:26:49.850
CHAPTER 4
A LONG DREAM

01:26:49.890 --> 01:26:52.320
Long, long ago,

01:26:53.860 --> 01:26:59.180
before anything besides inert matter
existed in this universe...

01:27:02.430 --> 01:27:07.850
All manner of insignificant things
came into and out of being.

01:27:08.500 --> 01:27:12.560
Eventually, something survived.

01:27:15.150 --> 01:27:17.670
We call that thing "life."

01:27:21.010 --> 01:27:28.360
In the end, the reason life survived
was that it had the ability to multiply.

01:27:29.710 --> 01:27:33.910
In order to multiply,
life kept changing form

01:27:33.910 --> 01:27:36.630
and adapted to any environment.

01:27:36.630 --> 01:27:38.930
And that led to us as we are today.

01:27:39.930 --> 01:27:44.510
Growing more numerous,
more widespread, more abundant...

01:27:44.890 --> 01:27:48.810
In other words, the objective
of living is to multiply.

01:27:49.520 --> 01:27:53.480
This sand, the pebbles, the water...

01:27:53.480 --> 01:27:55.310
none of them attempt to multiply.

01:27:55.900 --> 01:27:59.870
However, life is still doing
whatever it can to proliferate.

01:28:00.530 --> 01:28:06.360
Considering that death and extinction
run counter to the goal of multiplying,

01:28:06.360 --> 01:28:09.920
we are deterred from meeting our end
by the punishment known as fear.

01:28:10.230 --> 01:28:15.000
Like any of us, she did whatever she could
to escape the pain of experiencing it.

01:28:15.830 --> 01:28:20.750
She created a stronger, bigger, immortal body,

01:28:20.750 --> 01:28:25.640
and then she escaped into a world
where death doesn't even exist.

01:28:26.200 --> 01:28:31.360
That is the truth about the Founder Ymir, and
this is the world where death doesn't exist.

01:28:32.480 --> 01:28:37.150
If that's the case, then I wonder...
What on earth is Ymir's objective?

01:28:37.980 --> 01:28:39.570
I wondered that, too.

01:28:39.570 --> 01:28:44.410
I spent a maddening amount of time
here trying to understand her.

01:28:44.930 --> 01:28:51.340
Even with all this power,
she couldn't defy King Fritz.

01:28:52.250 --> 01:28:59.050
What would make her stay here for 2,000
long years, obeying King Fritz all the while?

01:29:02.820 --> 01:29:06.720
There was something she couldn't
let go of. That much is clear.

01:29:07.540 --> 01:29:12.810
Eren managed to understand
what it was, but I failed.

01:29:13.380 --> 01:29:16.890
And so, Ymir sided with Eren.

01:29:17.770 --> 01:29:22.400
I need you to tell me something. How does
one return to the outside world from here?

01:29:23.140 --> 01:29:24.950
Who knows?

01:29:24.950 --> 01:29:27.150
Personally, I don't think it's possible.

01:29:27.900 --> 01:29:30.660
I haven't given up on anything.

01:29:32.170 --> 01:29:33.540
Why?

01:29:33.540 --> 01:29:36.080
Uh, because...

01:29:36.080 --> 01:29:37.960
To keep multiplying?

01:29:38.460 --> 01:29:43.670
Is continuing the species
that important to you?

01:29:44.470 --> 01:29:50.200
You could call what's happening right now
the tragedy of life's being ruled by fear.

01:29:50.730 --> 01:29:56.230
A calamity of fear brought about
by the meaningless activities of life.

01:29:56.230 --> 01:29:58.640
My comrades are fighting!

01:29:58.640 --> 01:30:02.690
It's not too late to save
a lot of people from fear!

01:30:03.030 --> 01:30:05.070
They're fighting their fear!

01:30:05.860 --> 01:30:08.110
Why would it be bad to lose?

01:30:08.820 --> 01:30:12.500
Being alive means dying eventually.

01:30:16.430 --> 01:30:21.320
The moment before death
might just bring relief.

01:30:22.380 --> 01:30:29.640
No longer being driven solely to multiply,
never knowing what the point of it all is...

01:30:30.290 --> 01:30:33.890
It might feel like being set free.

01:30:43.990 --> 01:30:45.980
It was as the sun was setting...

01:30:46.530 --> 01:30:51.290
I was racing Eren and Mikasa...
racing to the tree on the hill.

01:30:53.080 --> 01:30:56.120
Eren started running the moment
after he suggested the race,

01:30:56.120 --> 01:30:59.170
and Mikasa deliberately lagged behind him.

01:30:59.630 --> 01:31:01.500
Of course, I was last.

01:31:01.960 --> 01:31:05.840
But the wind that day was slightly warm,

01:31:05.840 --> 01:31:08.550
and it felt so good just running.

01:31:09.680 --> 01:31:11.810
The wind stirred up
all the dead leaves.

01:31:12.390 --> 01:31:16.180
In that moment, the thought
entered my head

01:31:17.260 --> 01:31:23.150
that maybe I had been born
to race Mikasa and Eren up this hill.

01:31:26.020 --> 01:31:30.080
When I would read inside on rainy days,

01:31:30.660 --> 01:31:33.870
when I fed acorns to a squirrel,

01:31:34.330 --> 01:31:36.700
and when we walked around the market together,

01:31:37.200 --> 01:31:38.780
I felt the same way.

01:31:39.170 --> 01:31:43.540
I had the sense that these insignificant
moments were incredibly precious.

01:31:43.540 --> 01:31:44.790
Where'd you get that?

01:31:46.380 --> 01:31:48.790
I found it buried in the sand.

01:31:49.540 --> 01:31:51.550
Why would that be here?

01:31:52.180 --> 01:31:53.720
Who can say?

01:31:53.720 --> 01:31:59.440
But even though this isn't needed
to multiply or for anything else,

01:31:59.810 --> 01:32:02.980
to me, it's an incredibly precious thing.

01:32:04.900 --> 01:32:07.440
Oh, that's right.

01:32:08.810 --> 01:32:12.700
We would just throw the ball,
and catch it, and then throw it again.

01:32:13.410 --> 01:32:15.950
Just that. Over and over.

01:32:20.790 --> 01:32:22.670
There was no point to it.

01:32:23.250 --> 01:32:25.080
But it's as you say.

01:32:25.710 --> 01:32:30.260
I would've been happy
just playing catch forever.

01:32:43.980 --> 01:32:44.980
Pieck!

01:32:48.270 --> 01:32:50.360
I can still fight once my arm heals!

01:32:50.360 --> 01:32:53.360
We've reached our limit!
Let's retreat to Reiner's position!

01:32:56.320 --> 01:32:57.630
Reiner!

01:32:59.570 --> 01:33:00.750
Jean! Pieck!

01:33:06.460 --> 01:33:07.580
Annie!

01:33:25.020 --> 01:33:26.520
What's this?

01:33:33.290 --> 01:33:35.530
Porco! Marcel!

01:33:41.620 --> 01:33:42.660
Ymir!

01:33:43.460 --> 01:33:47.290
Did he... Did B-Bertholdt save us?

01:33:47.590 --> 01:33:49.000
I don't understand it.

01:33:49.000 --> 01:33:49.800
But...

01:33:49.800 --> 01:33:51.880
I won't let this chance slip away!

01:33:59.010 --> 01:34:00.140
I hit it!

01:34:05.640 --> 01:34:07.140
Give Armin...

01:34:08.140 --> 01:34:10.900
back!

01:34:18.070 --> 01:34:19.030
Armin!

01:34:28.910 --> 01:34:29.840
Annie!

01:34:38.920 --> 01:34:40.090
Annie?

01:34:41.850 --> 01:34:43.020
Armin...

01:34:44.270 --> 01:34:46.180
I'm sorry, everyone.

01:34:47.560 --> 01:34:50.480
But I'm fine now.

01:34:51.150 --> 01:34:52.820
Annie, behind you!

01:35:06.330 --> 01:35:09.380
What's going on? Titans are saving them?!

01:35:09.380 --> 01:35:11.170
Looks like it.

01:35:11.170 --> 01:35:13.380
Heeey!

01:35:13.880 --> 01:35:16.380
Heeey!

01:35:17.380 --> 01:35:19.890
Over here!

01:35:21.330 --> 01:35:22.390
It can't be...

01:35:22.390 --> 01:35:26.510
I'm the one you wanted to see, right, Levi?

01:35:26.510 --> 01:35:29.400
I didn't want to see you, though!

01:35:30.350 --> 01:35:31.850
Zeke...

01:35:38.730 --> 01:35:40.990
What's going on here?

01:35:40.990 --> 01:35:42.910
It's all thanks to Zeke.

01:35:42.910 --> 01:35:44.120
To Zeke?

01:35:44.660 --> 01:35:49.580
He awakened our comrades in the Paths,
where there's no life or death.

01:35:50.250 --> 01:35:53.960
All Eldians are connected via the Paths.

01:35:54.460 --> 01:35:55.880
That's because, most likely,

01:35:56.600 --> 01:36:00.320
the Founder Ymir is seeking connection.

01:36:00.920 --> 01:36:03.200
She's searching for something from us.

01:36:06.200 --> 01:36:07.600
Bertholdt...

01:36:12.450 --> 01:36:16.890
Mr. Ksaver, our dream didn't come to fruition.

01:36:17.810 --> 01:36:22.160
I still believe the
euthanization plan was right.

01:36:22.670 --> 01:36:23.530
But...

01:36:24.370 --> 01:36:27.070
If it meant I could play catch with you,

01:36:27.070 --> 01:36:30.750
I wouldn't mind being born again.

01:36:33.040 --> 01:36:39.130
So, I'll thank you for that at least, Father.

01:36:40.800 --> 01:36:43.980
I took everything from you.

01:36:44.570 --> 01:36:48.860
Your life, your power,
and even your treasured memories.

01:36:50.120 --> 01:36:51.340
Which is why...

01:36:51.340 --> 01:36:54.690
I already know that you don't
want to just stand here.

01:36:55.100 --> 01:36:56.060
All of you...

01:36:56.590 --> 01:36:58.410
Please lend us a hand!

01:37:06.630 --> 01:37:08.960
The weather's downright lovely.

01:37:10.750 --> 01:37:13.720
If I'd felt that way sooner...

01:37:14.200 --> 01:37:15.460
Well...

01:37:15.890 --> 01:37:20.020
After I killed so many people,
that'd be asking for too much, wouldn't it?

01:37:45.500 --> 01:37:48.630
The rumbling... stopped?

01:38:07.800 --> 01:38:09.840
Jean, go!

01:38:20.780 --> 01:38:21.780
Jean!

01:38:30.700 --> 01:38:32.040
You damned

01:38:32.040 --> 01:38:37.410
suicidal dumbass!

01:38:57.020 --> 01:38:59.690
That thing's gonna go for Eren's head again!

01:39:05.060 --> 01:39:05.940
Reiner!

01:39:05.940 --> 01:39:06.820
Jean! Pieck!

01:39:07.230 --> 01:39:10.580
We're getting out of here!
Armin's gonna blow all of this up!

01:39:10.910 --> 01:39:12.910
Wait! Reiner's down there!

01:39:12.910 --> 01:39:17.660
The Armored Titan should be able to
withstand the Colossal's explosion.

01:39:18.290 --> 01:39:23.460
Regardless, to pass up this chance
would be to trample on Reiner's resolve.

01:39:28.770 --> 01:39:29.950
Thank you.

01:39:33.060 --> 01:39:38.140
We couldn't have stopped the rumbling
without the help of all of you.

01:39:45.730 --> 01:39:49.710
Goodbye, Eren.

01:40:16.760 --> 01:40:19.100
Karina! Are you okay?

01:40:20.850 --> 01:40:22.360
What happened?

01:40:22.360 --> 01:40:24.150
That was a crazy explosion!

01:40:24.150 --> 01:40:25.270
Did everyone make it?

01:40:25.270 --> 01:40:26.360
Look!

01:40:30.220 --> 01:40:31.870
Look! The bones...

01:40:32.700 --> 01:40:33.910
Does that mean...

01:40:33.910 --> 01:40:35.320
Eren's dead?

01:40:40.460 --> 01:40:46.210
Ackermanns with awakened powers
apparently get sudden headaches.

01:40:46.210 --> 01:40:48.670
That... was the last time we spoke?

01:40:49.590 --> 01:40:53.260
... Mikasa, I've hated you.

01:40:53.260 --> 01:40:55.070
That can't be...

01:41:14.430 --> 01:41:16.980
I can't say I don't have regrets.

01:41:18.190 --> 01:41:22.120
Still, what we did was right, wasn't it?

01:41:22.580 --> 01:41:24.670
We did stop the rumbling.

01:41:25.330 --> 01:41:28.620
You came here from the internment zone? How?

01:41:29.180 --> 01:41:30.800
It was Mr. Leonhart.

01:41:30.800 --> 01:41:33.340
He led us this far.

01:41:34.380 --> 01:41:35.660
Go see him, dear.

01:41:43.560 --> 01:41:44.730
Armin!

01:41:44.730 --> 01:41:45.810
Do you see Reiner?

01:41:55.400 --> 01:41:56.570
- Reiner!
- He's okay!

01:41:56.860 --> 01:41:59.070
Hey! Look over there!

01:42:02.080 --> 01:42:05.080
It's still alive,
even after taking that blast?!

01:42:05.080 --> 01:42:07.460
What on earth is it?

01:42:07.460 --> 01:42:08.790
Beats me.

01:42:08.790 --> 01:42:12.840
But I do know we can't let it live.

01:42:22.850 --> 01:42:25.040
Well, that figures.

01:42:25.390 --> 01:42:28.390
I didn't think that'd be enough to kill you.

01:42:28.390 --> 01:42:31.570
Yeah... But what do we do?

01:42:34.150 --> 01:42:35.280
Eren.

01:42:42.500 --> 01:42:43.510
This is bad!

01:42:43.510 --> 01:42:47.500
If the glowing thing and Eren come into
contact, the rumbling might start again!

01:42:47.500 --> 01:42:50.260
Yeah. We gotta kill it.

01:42:50.260 --> 01:42:53.960
How're we gonna kill something
that survived a blast like that?

01:42:53.960 --> 01:42:55.260
The one we should target

01:42:55.260 --> 01:42:56.600
is Eren.

01:42:57.260 --> 01:42:58.800
You've caught on, right?

01:42:59.210 --> 01:43:03.180
This nightmare won't end
until we take him down.

01:43:03.810 --> 01:43:07.020
Dad, I have one last job to do.

01:43:07.470 --> 01:43:11.030
I'll see this through. For Colt's sake, too.

01:43:11.820 --> 01:43:13.070
Why?

01:43:13.530 --> 01:43:16.230
Why did it turn out this way?

01:43:28.730 --> 01:43:30.610
Did you hurt your leg?

01:43:31.750 --> 01:43:35.960
No, it was already like this. Thanks.

01:43:37.300 --> 01:43:38.460
Bring the injured here!

01:43:38.460 --> 01:43:45.190
If you hadn't emptied your gun into the air,
we would've still been fighting each other.

01:43:45.970 --> 01:43:48.600
I've made more than enough mistakes.

01:43:48.970 --> 01:43:51.690
Let's work together and overcome this.

01:43:51.690 --> 01:43:52.360
Agreed.

01:43:52.360 --> 01:43:53.320
Dad!

01:43:57.230 --> 01:43:59.230
A-Annie?

01:44:04.740 --> 01:44:07.910
This vapor is coming from the glowing thing!

01:44:07.910 --> 01:44:09.370
Did it die?

01:44:09.370 --> 01:44:12.750
No... It doesn't smell like when Titans die.

01:44:14.340 --> 01:44:18.630
Could it be... What if it's like the stuff
that was used on Ragako Village?

01:44:19.380 --> 01:44:20.050
What?

01:44:20.050 --> 01:44:21.350
Mikasa! Pieck!

01:44:21.350 --> 01:44:23.720
Get on Falco! We're getting out of here!

01:44:23.720 --> 01:44:26.260
Huh? What are you talking about?

01:44:26.740 --> 01:44:29.770
Ackermanns and Titan wielders
are immune, remember?

01:44:30.230 --> 01:44:33.560
You know better than anyone
what we've gotta do!

01:44:34.690 --> 01:44:35.940
But that...

01:44:36.480 --> 01:44:37.730
No...

01:44:38.240 --> 01:44:39.520
It's too much...

01:44:39.520 --> 01:44:40.620
Right now! Go!

01:44:45.620 --> 01:44:46.780
No!

01:44:46.780 --> 01:44:49.750
Dad!

01:45:03.970 --> 01:45:06.400
So this is how we go out.

01:45:07.430 --> 01:45:08.800
Guess so.

01:45:09.340 --> 01:45:11.310
We'll entrust the rest to our comrades.

01:45:11.310 --> 01:45:15.270
That's how Scout Regiment
soldiers meet their end.

01:45:16.400 --> 01:45:21.410
Do you remember, Jean?
The night we burned the corpses.

01:45:21.860 --> 01:45:22.780
Yeah.

01:45:23.240 --> 01:45:27.280
This was all your fault, you know.

01:45:27.280 --> 01:45:30.540
That we got stuck
with having to save humanity.

01:45:41.250 --> 01:45:42.300
This is absurd.

01:45:42.930 --> 01:45:46.300
How can something like this be happening?

01:45:47.180 --> 01:45:50.060
Hey! Hey! Annie!

01:45:50.520 --> 01:45:51.560
Are you all right?

01:45:51.980 --> 01:45:53.810
What on earth happened?

01:45:58.060 --> 01:45:59.640
S-Secretary!

01:46:25.510 --> 01:46:28.840
The bastard summoned an army.

01:46:29.340 --> 01:46:31.100
Damn it! Enough already!

01:46:31.560 --> 01:46:33.850
I'm not gonna let you pass!

01:46:36.730 --> 01:46:41.240
You really enjoy hell, don't you, Eren?

01:46:41.860 --> 01:46:45.490
Fine. We'll do things your way.

01:46:45.490 --> 01:46:47.610
I'll see this through to the very end!

01:46:59.880 --> 01:47:02.380
Conny? Jean? Gabi?

01:47:03.960 --> 01:47:05.210
It can't be...

01:47:05.210 --> 01:47:06.130
How?

01:47:06.800 --> 01:47:08.130
Mom?

01:47:13.100 --> 01:47:14.140
Pieck!

01:47:14.560 --> 01:47:15.640
Annie!

01:47:22.490 --> 01:47:26.890
When will our torment end?

01:47:28.880 --> 01:47:30.040
Mikasa?

01:47:31.040 --> 01:47:32.540
Pull it together!

01:47:32.540 --> 01:47:35.580
We're the only ones who can kill Eren now!

01:47:37.230 --> 01:47:39.660
It's too much...

01:47:40.690 --> 01:47:42.310
I can't take any more.

01:47:44.300 --> 01:47:45.710
I wanna go back.

01:47:48.940 --> 01:47:52.980
I wanna go back to our home.

01:47:56.420 --> 01:47:59.260
Mikasa. Wake up.

01:48:01.650 --> 01:48:02.830
You'll catch a cold.

01:48:04.020 --> 01:48:05.320
Eren?

01:48:06.070 --> 01:48:07.020
Huh?

01:48:07.020 --> 01:48:11.240
When did I fall asleep?

01:48:15.830 --> 01:48:18.450
You must have been exhausted.

01:48:20.330 --> 01:48:24.370
It's just, I feel like I had
a really long dream.

01:48:24.840 --> 01:48:28.500
Let's just take it easy and do nothing
for the rest of the day.

01:48:29.000 --> 01:48:31.350
I caught some huge fish, so—

01:48:32.640 --> 01:48:33.850
Mikasa?

01:48:34.510 --> 01:48:35.890
Why are you crying?

01:48:35.890 --> 01:48:36.890
Huh?

01:48:39.300 --> 01:48:40.860
I don't know.

01:48:41.940 --> 01:48:46.730
I suddenly felt like I shouldn't be here.

01:48:48.870 --> 01:48:52.210
There's nothing we can do anymore.

01:48:52.990 --> 01:48:53.870
Huh?

01:48:54.330 --> 01:49:00.000
That day, we cast everything aside
to run away to this place.

01:49:03.100 --> 01:49:05.520
Two months after the end of Marley's war,

01:49:06.130 --> 01:49:08.920
an invasion of Paradis Island
was on the horizon.

01:49:10.270 --> 01:49:12.380
If we hadn't run, they would've killed us all.

01:49:13.120 --> 01:49:16.820
I'm sure Armin has been desperate to find us.

01:49:18.890 --> 01:49:23.940
I couldn't bring myself to plunge Historia into
hell and commit to an endless cycle of killing,

01:49:24.670 --> 01:49:27.950
and I couldn't bring genocide
upon all humanity outside the island.

01:49:29.850 --> 01:49:31.410
So let's just go

01:49:32.200 --> 01:49:35.010
live out my remaining four years
in peace and quiet...

01:49:35.640 --> 01:49:38.860
Just the two of us, somewhere
with no other people.

01:49:39.990 --> 01:49:43.130
You're the one who said all that, Mikasa.

01:49:43.130 --> 01:49:44.500
It was your idea.

01:49:47.990 --> 01:49:49.090
Yeah.

01:49:53.140 --> 01:49:54.460
I'm sorry.

01:49:55.010 --> 01:49:57.540
I know we promised we
wouldn't talk about that stuff.

01:49:59.580 --> 01:50:02.650
Can we make another promise?

01:50:04.090 --> 01:50:08.020
Once I'm dead, throw this scarf away.

01:50:08.960 --> 01:50:13.030
You're going to live a long time after this.

01:50:14.270 --> 01:50:15.940
Forget all about me.

01:50:16.750 --> 01:50:18.280
Forget, and be free.

01:50:23.760 --> 01:50:25.360
Please, Mikasa.

01:50:26.960 --> 01:50:28.410
Forget about me.

01:50:50.430 --> 01:50:51.440
I'm sorry.

01:50:54.530 --> 01:50:55.940
I can't.

01:50:57.860 --> 01:50:59.690
Eren is in the mouth!

01:51:01.540 --> 01:51:04.040
Everyone, help me get there!

01:51:04.040 --> 01:51:05.770
Roger that, Mikasa!

01:51:08.580 --> 01:51:10.220
Eren!

01:52:18.070 --> 01:52:21.990
I'll see you later, Eren.

01:52:42.850 --> 01:52:45.020
FINAL CHAPTER

01:52:45.020 --> 01:52:52.860
FINAL CHAPTER
TOWARD THE TREE ON THAT HILL

01:52:57.150 --> 01:53:02.370
I get that it was for the sake of the future
you saw with the Attack Titan's ability,

01:53:02.870 --> 01:53:06.740
but did you absolutely have to
beat me up that badly?

01:53:06.740 --> 01:53:10.120
Was the knee to the stomach really necessary?

01:53:10.790 --> 01:53:13.880
I was doing whatever I could
to push you two away.

01:53:13.880 --> 01:53:17.360
It seemed kinda crazy to me, too.

01:53:18.090 --> 01:53:20.640
I let myself get carried away.

01:53:22.340 --> 01:53:23.930
I'm really sorry.

01:53:23.930 --> 01:53:27.390
Don't apologize to me. Apologize to Mikasa.

01:53:27.390 --> 01:53:29.890
She's the one you hurt with your nonsense.

01:53:30.560 --> 01:53:33.500
Yeah, you're right.

01:53:35.250 --> 01:53:38.270
It was all to push us away,

01:53:38.270 --> 01:53:44.410
and make us into the heroes who killed you
and saved humanity from annihilation?

01:53:44.740 --> 01:53:50.160
That's right. Every surviving human
would owe you a debt of gratitude.

01:53:50.750 --> 01:53:55.810
Island devils who went against the island
and stayed true to the path of humanity.

01:53:57.300 --> 01:54:00.840
It would make you the most
respected individuals in the world.

01:54:01.220 --> 01:54:05.220
So you're telling us to protect Paradis
from reprisal by the rest of the world,

01:54:05.220 --> 01:54:08.930
like the Tybur family
after the Great Titan War?

01:54:11.580 --> 01:54:14.320
There's no way we can become heroes, Eren.

01:54:15.400 --> 01:54:16.770
Sorry to disappoint you,

01:54:16.770 --> 01:54:21.700
but neither I nor the others intend
to play the hero like you want.

01:54:24.490 --> 01:54:25.700
Where're you going?

01:54:26.400 --> 01:54:28.610
The places we wanted to go.

01:54:28.920 --> 01:54:30.460
While we walk, I'll tell you...

01:54:31.490 --> 01:54:33.460
about the Founder Ymir.

01:54:46.630 --> 01:54:49.760
So this is that "fiery water"?

01:54:50.220 --> 01:54:54.090
It really is flowing like a river.

01:54:59.230 --> 01:55:00.990
Where did I leave off?

01:55:00.990 --> 01:55:02.240
Huh?

01:55:02.240 --> 01:55:04.440
You said the power of the Titans still exists

01:55:04.440 --> 01:55:09.820
because the Founder Ymir has continued
to obey King Fritz for 2,000 years.

01:55:09.820 --> 01:55:11.000
Right.

01:55:11.000 --> 01:55:15.000
He burned down her home, killed her parents,
and ripped out her tongue,

01:55:15.580 --> 01:55:18.410
and yet even after attaining godlike power,

01:55:18.410 --> 01:55:20.330
she remained subservient to him.

01:55:20.330 --> 01:55:24.010
What in the world made her do that?

01:55:24.670 --> 01:55:28.160
There's something I felt
when I touched her in the Paths.

01:55:28.710 --> 01:55:30.520
I couldn't believe it.

01:55:31.190 --> 01:55:32.770
The Founder Ymir...

01:55:33.490 --> 01:55:35.870
loved King Fritz.

01:55:36.430 --> 01:55:37.520
What?

01:55:37.520 --> 01:55:42.690
That's what it was that kept Ymir bound,
even after 2,000 years.

01:55:46.320 --> 01:55:50.300
I can't understand the deepest depths
of the Founder Ymir's heart.

01:55:51.650 --> 01:55:55.240
But it was clear that she'd been suffering

01:55:55.860 --> 01:55:57.450
for the entire 2,000 years.

01:55:58.370 --> 01:56:03.550
She kept searching for someone to
release her, and finally, they appeared.

01:56:05.320 --> 01:56:06.860
That person was Mikasa.

01:56:10.810 --> 01:56:12.850
What?! Did you just say "Mikasa"?!

01:56:12.850 --> 01:56:15.850
I did. So you weren't listening after all.

01:56:15.850 --> 01:56:17.100
I was listening!

01:56:18.560 --> 01:56:21.110
Why Mikasa?

01:56:21.440 --> 01:56:23.170
Well...

01:56:23.170 --> 01:56:25.980
Only the Founder Ymir knows that.

01:56:26.530 --> 01:56:30.510
I still don't know what Mikasa did.

01:56:31.660 --> 01:56:36.430
What I knew for certain is that
the outcome Mikasa brought about...

01:56:37.260 --> 01:56:41.010
is what I kept moving forward to reach.

01:56:42.130 --> 01:56:46.710
I slaughtered humanity, caused
Eldians to kill each other on Paradis,

01:56:46.710 --> 01:56:50.730
and dragged my dear friends into combat,

01:56:50.730 --> 01:56:55.890
without ever knowing
whether they'd survive.

01:56:57.580 --> 01:57:00.850
That's the future you saw
at the medal ceremony...

01:57:01.400 --> 01:57:02.560
Armin,

01:57:03.780 --> 01:57:06.700
my head has become a total mess.

01:57:07.110 --> 01:57:11.280
One of the effects of the Founding Titan's power
is that there's no "past" or "future."

01:57:11.280 --> 01:57:13.160
It all exists simultaneously.

01:57:13.680 --> 01:57:16.910
And so... I had no choice.

01:57:17.660 --> 01:57:23.420
That day, in that moment,
Bertholdt had to stay alive.

01:57:23.890 --> 01:57:24.920
Huh?

01:57:25.270 --> 01:57:27.420
So I... sent it

01:57:28.460 --> 01:57:30.800
toward my mom and not him.

01:57:34.670 --> 01:57:36.970
Let's go, Eren.

01:57:39.520 --> 01:57:40.730
Okay.

01:57:44.170 --> 01:57:47.060
So, how did it go?

01:57:47.480 --> 01:57:48.520
What do you mean?

01:57:48.520 --> 01:57:50.230
With Mikasa!

01:57:50.540 --> 01:57:55.080
Do you think she's gonna be able to forget
about you and live happily with someone else?

01:57:55.080 --> 01:57:57.410
The way you wanted.

01:57:57.410 --> 01:57:59.490
Mmh. Dunno.

01:58:06.210 --> 01:58:07.080
Ow...

01:58:07.080 --> 01:58:08.750
The hell kind of answer is that?

01:58:08.750 --> 01:58:10.500
I still haven't forgiven you!

01:58:10.500 --> 01:58:14.430
How do you feel about the fact
that you ignored Mikasa's feelings?

01:58:14.430 --> 01:58:17.550
Mikasa risked her life
and only ever had eyes for you!

01:58:17.910 --> 01:58:21.020
Did you think you could just say
"forget about me" and that'd be that?!

01:58:23.020 --> 01:58:28.730
At the very least, Mikasa should forget about
a heartbreaker like you and find happiness.

01:58:28.730 --> 01:58:33.900
Well, she just might find a good guy sooner
than you'd think and hit it off with him.

01:58:35.450 --> 01:58:36.490
No...

01:58:37.280 --> 01:58:38.860
That'd kill me!

01:58:38.860 --> 01:58:40.920
I don't want her to find someone.

01:58:41.280 --> 01:58:43.870
I want to be her one and only
for the rest of my life!

01:58:43.870 --> 01:58:48.540
And after I die, I want her to
pine after me for at least ten years!

01:58:50.880 --> 01:58:53.070
Oh... I see...

01:58:53.630 --> 01:58:57.340
I didn't think you'd
say anything that pathetic...

01:58:57.340 --> 01:59:00.050
Don't tell Mikasa any of this.

01:59:01.850 --> 01:59:04.950
I want her to find happiness. I really do.

01:59:05.560 --> 01:59:09.510
But I... Ugh, damn it!

01:59:10.310 --> 01:59:12.400
I don't wanna die.

01:59:12.840 --> 01:59:17.320
I don't wanna leave Mikasa, or any of you!

01:59:18.020 --> 01:59:21.590
Eren! Let's keep trying!
Let's find another way!

01:59:21.590 --> 01:59:22.570
We can't!

01:59:22.920 --> 01:59:25.770
I'm sure none of them wanted to die, either.

01:59:26.420 --> 01:59:29.330
And yet... I...

01:59:40.170 --> 01:59:41.720
Eighty percent.

01:59:42.600 --> 01:59:43.600
What?

01:59:43.890 --> 01:59:47.100
I trample eighty percent of humanity.

01:59:51.360 --> 01:59:53.860
How could you?!

01:59:54.190 --> 01:59:56.440
Eren! Why?

01:59:56.980 --> 02:00:01.580
I attempt a complete eradication
of humanity outside the walls,

02:00:02.080 --> 02:00:03.950
and all of you stop me.

02:00:03.950 --> 02:00:06.290
And ultimately, eighty percent die.

02:00:06.870 --> 02:00:11.710
The world outside the walls drops
to the same level of civilization as Paradis.

02:00:11.710 --> 02:00:16.520
Which means there won't be
a one-sided war of reprisal,

02:00:16.940 --> 02:00:19.210
but this conflict doesn't end.

02:00:20.340 --> 02:00:22.250
What the hell do you mean?

02:00:22.880 --> 02:00:26.010
Are you trying to say what
we've done is all pointless?

02:00:26.010 --> 02:00:29.350
The massacre hasn't occurred yet!
Just stop it!

02:00:29.620 --> 02:00:30.980
I can't.

02:00:31.530 --> 02:00:34.830
Twenty percent of humanity
is all you manage to save.

02:00:35.610 --> 02:00:37.980
It's already been determined.

02:00:37.980 --> 02:00:40.190
"Been determined"?

02:00:40.190 --> 02:00:43.240
Didn't you determine it?
Didn't you kill them?

02:00:44.060 --> 02:00:48.700
So, so many times I tested it,
all to no avail.

02:00:49.490 --> 02:00:53.960
Things always occurred exactly as I saw
in my memories of the future.

02:00:54.900 --> 02:00:58.460
Armin, it's just as you said.

02:00:58.460 --> 02:01:01.960
I'm... a slave to freedom.

02:01:03.760 --> 02:01:08.120
This is... absolutely crazy!

02:01:08.920 --> 02:01:12.190
You're saying... it can't be undone?

02:01:12.770 --> 02:01:14.610
This can't be!

02:01:15.020 --> 02:01:17.400
This isn't a solution at all!

02:01:17.400 --> 02:01:20.480
What, you can't have war
if there are no people?

02:01:20.480 --> 02:01:22.910
It's like a bad joke!
Who would take it seriously?

02:01:23.780 --> 02:01:28.610
Eren, it's true that there's no
end in sight for this conflict,

02:01:28.610 --> 02:01:33.920
and I'm sure the hell we went through
has happened over and over.

02:01:34.710 --> 02:01:37.080
But we need to think
that despite it all, one day,

02:01:37.920 --> 02:01:42.010
we can eventually come
to understand one another...

02:01:42.350 --> 02:01:48.930
And now no one will have any faith,
not even in something as small as that!

02:01:50.340 --> 02:01:52.560
The only lesson they'll be left with...

02:01:52.560 --> 02:01:54.600
is that they must kill, or be killed.

02:01:54.980 --> 02:01:56.440
That's all.

02:01:58.020 --> 02:02:02.450
And you're saying you did all this for us?

02:02:03.700 --> 02:02:04.700
Eren.

02:02:05.240 --> 02:02:06.780
That's your name.

02:02:07.170 --> 02:02:08.910
No. I didn't.

02:02:10.720 --> 02:02:15.170
Eren, you're free.

02:02:19.330 --> 02:02:23.380
I wanted to level everything.

02:02:25.580 --> 02:02:27.630
I wanted to see this sight.

02:02:28.930 --> 02:02:30.060
Why?

02:02:31.230 --> 02:02:35.890
I don't know why. I just wanted to do it...

02:02:35.890 --> 02:02:37.640
so very badly.

02:02:41.660 --> 02:02:45.530
I thought I was doing everything
to protect all of you.

02:02:45.530 --> 02:02:49.530
But Sasha and Hange died because of me,

02:02:49.990 --> 02:02:53.050
and I wound up putting you
in lethal confrontations with Floch.

02:02:54.540 --> 02:02:55.910
Why...

02:02:56.370 --> 02:02:58.500
Why did it turn out this way?

02:02:58.970 --> 02:03:00.920
I finally know.

02:03:01.840 --> 02:03:04.050
It's because I'm an idiot.

02:03:04.590 --> 02:03:08.750
A garden-variety idiot
who got his hands on power.

02:03:09.630 --> 02:03:13.130
That's why this resolution
was the only possible outcome.

02:03:14.560 --> 02:03:16.620
That's all there is to it, right?

02:03:29.110 --> 02:03:30.280
I get it.

02:03:31.660 --> 02:03:35.200
Wanting to erase people from the world...

02:03:35.750 --> 02:03:36.950
I've felt that way, too.

02:03:38.290 --> 02:03:41.170
Liar. You would never—

02:03:41.170 --> 02:03:42.960
Nobody would guess it,

02:03:43.340 --> 02:03:46.300
considering I'm a hero who saved
twenty percent of humanity.

02:03:46.300 --> 02:03:50.800
Still, it was me that showed you
the book about the outside world.

02:03:51.260 --> 02:03:55.220
The one who put the idea of a free,
unoccupied world in your head

02:03:55.960 --> 02:03:57.070
was me.

02:03:58.180 --> 02:03:59.470
What's that?

02:03:59.970 --> 02:04:02.280
So you finally noticed it.

02:04:02.280 --> 02:04:04.480
It was at our feet the whole time,

02:04:04.920 --> 02:04:07.560
but you were always looking off
into the distance.

02:04:09.070 --> 02:04:11.240
Thank you, Eren.

02:04:11.960 --> 02:04:16.220
For showing me what was beyond the walls.
For showing me this sight.

02:04:17.330 --> 02:04:19.510
We did this.

02:04:20.200 --> 02:04:24.960
So after this we'll be
together forever, won't we?

02:04:25.630 --> 02:04:28.460
After this? Where?

02:04:28.800 --> 02:04:31.680
In hell, assuming it exists.

02:04:31.680 --> 02:04:35.350
We'll suffer for the sin of killing
eighty percent of humanity.

02:04:36.320 --> 02:04:37.430
Together.

02:04:47.640 --> 02:04:49.810
Armin, it's time.

02:04:50.210 --> 02:04:52.460
I'm erasing your memory of our time here,

02:04:52.810 --> 02:04:55.700
but once everything is over,
you'll remember again.

02:04:55.990 --> 02:04:57.030
I know.

02:04:57.030 --> 02:04:58.950
Our next meeting will be
a fight to the death.

02:04:59.780 --> 02:05:01.960
And the next one after that...

02:05:03.090 --> 02:05:04.170
Yeah.

02:05:05.220 --> 02:05:07.000
I'll be waiting for you.

02:05:07.380 --> 02:05:08.630
In hell.

02:05:09.460 --> 02:05:14.920
Right. We'll be together, forever.

02:05:18.890 --> 02:05:20.980
Are your wounds healed now?

02:05:20.980 --> 02:05:23.980
Huh? Annie?

02:05:25.540 --> 02:05:28.450
Yeah, since we've had some time...

02:05:52.680 --> 02:05:55.550
I remember now. I...

02:05:56.350 --> 02:05:57.440
Armin.

02:06:15.820 --> 02:06:18.250
You got your memories back too, right?

02:06:19.280 --> 02:06:22.080
Of the times Eren came to see us.

02:06:22.960 --> 02:06:24.120
Yeah.

02:06:24.620 --> 02:06:29.580
He told me that the outcome
you bring about through your choices

02:06:30.200 --> 02:06:35.380
is to erase the Power of
the Titans from the world.

02:06:36.760 --> 02:06:41.100
I remember now, you damned
conscientious dumbass.

02:06:41.690 --> 02:06:45.350
Eren, I can't believe you...

02:06:45.940 --> 02:06:51.860
Listen to this: Eren said my mom
would turn back into a human.

02:06:52.280 --> 02:06:56.840
He... told us to live a long life.

02:06:58.100 --> 02:06:59.740
But what about you?

02:06:59.740 --> 02:07:03.970
Worry about yourself, you suicidal maniac.

02:07:05.490 --> 02:07:06.710
Is that so?

02:07:07.780 --> 02:07:11.760
I wish I'd gotten to chat with him.

02:07:15.550 --> 02:07:17.510
Welcome home.

02:07:18.130 --> 02:07:21.520
I'm home, Dad.

02:07:21.520 --> 02:07:24.530
Gabi!

02:07:27.080 --> 02:07:29.520
Look who showed up.

02:07:30.980 --> 02:07:32.870
Were you watching?

02:07:34.440 --> 02:07:36.650
Seems this was the resolution

02:07:37.610 --> 02:07:41.160
that you gave your hearts for.

02:08:10.850 --> 02:08:12.040
Sasha?

02:08:15.440 --> 02:08:18.260
Mom! Dad!

02:08:19.730 --> 02:08:21.790
Gabi!

02:08:21.790 --> 02:08:22.700
Falco!

02:08:29.890 --> 02:08:31.300
Mom...

02:08:32.210 --> 02:08:37.300
I'm apparently not
the Armored Titan anymore.

02:08:38.350 --> 02:08:39.760
Really?

02:08:40.800 --> 02:08:42.560
I'm glad.

02:08:42.560 --> 02:08:43.220
What?

02:08:43.220 --> 02:08:47.060
All this time... I'm so sorry, Reiner.

02:08:48.140 --> 02:08:51.690
You were all I ever needed.

02:08:58.520 --> 02:09:00.570
I'll be going now.

02:09:00.920 --> 02:09:02.950
Huh? Where?

02:09:03.510 --> 02:09:09.450
If I stay here, I'm sure Eren
won't be allowed a proper burial.

02:09:10.410 --> 02:09:11.960
Good point.

02:09:14.670 --> 02:09:18.710
Put him to rest in a nice, quiet place.

02:09:25.480 --> 02:09:29.090
You know, the place where Eren
was always taking naps.

02:09:30.400 --> 02:09:33.290
Yeah. I think that's a good spot.

02:09:49.650 --> 02:09:51.770
Please listen, Secretary Müller.

02:09:52.380 --> 02:09:54.710
Eren Jaeger is dead.

02:09:54.710 --> 02:09:57.380
The Power of the Titans is gone, too!

02:09:58.040 --> 02:10:00.880
We're just regular people now!

02:10:01.390 --> 02:10:05.390
Can you prove that? Right here, right now?

02:10:11.730 --> 02:10:13.850
A blood test would—

02:10:13.850 --> 02:10:15.520
I said right here, right now!

02:10:15.930 --> 02:10:19.270
Please prove it to us.

02:10:19.940 --> 02:10:22.990
Whether you're human or Titan.

02:10:25.780 --> 02:10:31.290
If we still possessed Titan powers,
we'd use them to resist.

02:10:32.160 --> 02:10:37.290
But even with those barrels pointed at us,
we remain powerless.

02:10:37.290 --> 02:10:40.150
There's no greater proof that we're human.

02:10:41.440 --> 02:10:43.050
Who are you?

02:10:45.050 --> 02:10:49.050
Armin Arlelt, an Eldian from Paradis Island.

02:10:49.620 --> 02:10:53.720
I'm the one who killed
the Attack Titan, Eren Jaeger.

02:10:56.250 --> 02:10:57.730
It was you, wasn't it?

02:10:59.140 --> 02:11:02.260
The one who was peeking
into my head all this time.

02:11:04.480 --> 02:11:07.570
I think your love was nothing
but a long nightmare.

02:11:08.740 --> 02:11:11.330
The lives taken will never come back.

02:11:12.250 --> 02:11:18.330
Still, I exist because
of the lives you created.

02:11:27.650 --> 02:11:30.210
Rest in peace, Ymir.

02:12:01.950 --> 02:12:05.380
It's been three years since the day now known
as the "Battle of Heaven and Earth."

02:12:07.060 --> 02:12:09.770
After the loss of an extraordinary
number of lives,

02:12:11.090 --> 02:12:16.220
those who managed to survive surely
still suffer from unhealed wounds.

02:12:20.520 --> 02:12:24.070
Just as the world, still
reeling from the loss, feared,

02:12:24.070 --> 02:12:28.940
Eldia formed a military
led by the Jaegerists

02:12:28.940 --> 02:12:31.150
which gains strength with every passing day.

02:12:32.240 --> 02:12:36.370
Out of fear of reprisal from the
survivors of humanity across the sea,

02:12:36.370 --> 02:12:38.660
the island shouts with one voice:

02:12:39.660 --> 02:12:40.660
"If we win, we live."

02:12:41.500 --> 02:12:42.960
"If we lose, we die."

02:12:44.050 --> 02:12:46.000
"We have to fight to win."

02:12:46.670 --> 02:12:49.590
"Fight. Fight."

02:12:51.380 --> 02:12:55.100
Even with the Titans gone,
the conflict will not go away.

02:12:55.600 --> 02:12:58.970
Eren passed on to me
all that he knew of the future.

02:12:59.760 --> 02:13:03.440
Though I cannot see the future
that lies beyond this one,

02:13:03.440 --> 02:13:06.940
I have been able to see this future clearly.

02:13:07.520 --> 02:13:11.830
I'm certain this outcome was not
the result of Eren's choices alone.

02:13:12.350 --> 02:13:16.950
This world is an outcome
wrought by all of our choices.

02:13:17.950 --> 02:13:20.870
We must fight,

02:13:20.870 --> 02:13:23.040
so that we need fight no more.

02:13:23.450 --> 02:13:27.460
Even if we should find ourselves
living lives divorced from peace.

02:13:28.590 --> 02:13:32.260
This isn't the life he wished for us.

02:13:32.260 --> 02:13:36.260
But whether he wished for it or not,
it is the life he passed on to us.

02:13:37.390 --> 02:13:40.010
How will we live in
the reprieve that remains?

02:13:40.680 --> 02:13:41.480
In this...

02:13:42.110 --> 02:13:44.480
...world without Titans?

02:13:50.120 --> 02:13:53.570
I can't get over how beautiful
Historia's handwriting is.

02:13:55.360 --> 02:13:56.570
It even smells good.

02:13:56.570 --> 02:14:00.240
I'll repeat what I said before:
Don't lust after married women.

02:14:00.240 --> 02:14:01.710
It's creepy.

02:14:01.710 --> 02:14:06.130
I can't help but notice
your fixation with your hair.

02:14:06.130 --> 02:14:08.000
Who are you trying to look good for?

02:14:08.000 --> 02:14:11.510
The ladies who'll be reading
the history books in school.

02:14:11.970 --> 02:14:14.520
Don't you mean the field guide to horses?

02:14:14.520 --> 02:14:18.120
It's a real shame
your life got longer, Reiner.

02:14:18.800 --> 02:14:20.720
Paradis Island has come into view.

02:14:22.690 --> 02:14:26.270
Armin, do you really think this will work?

02:14:26.800 --> 02:14:29.650
We destroyed the walls,
betrayed the island,

02:14:30.190 --> 02:14:33.910
and killed Eren, whom the Eldians revere.

02:14:33.910 --> 02:14:37.320
Can we really be the Allied Forces'
ambassadors for the peace talks?

02:14:38.610 --> 02:14:42.920
I wouldn't be surprised if they
sank our ship right about now.

02:14:43.230 --> 02:14:46.670
Yeah, I'm amazed we're still afloat.

02:14:47.100 --> 02:14:51.290
This is the role of "international heroes"
that idiot forced on us.

02:14:52.220 --> 02:14:54.300
"I want you to have long lives," my ass.

02:14:54.300 --> 02:14:58.800
Annie, don't tell me you got on
this ship expecting to go home alive.

02:14:59.090 --> 02:15:04.810
Of course not. But it's not like any of us
came to commit suicide, right?

02:15:08.810 --> 02:15:12.360
Walking into hell again
like this is the answer.

02:15:13.330 --> 02:15:18.130
The Scout Regiment is made up of a bunch of
dreamers who don't know when to quit.

02:15:19.240 --> 02:15:20.860
I'm Military Police, though.

02:15:20.860 --> 02:15:23.330
But for the time being, we won't be killed.

02:15:24.210 --> 02:15:27.080
After all, everyone on Paradis
will want to know.

02:15:28.100 --> 02:15:30.310
To know our story.

02:15:49.130 --> 02:15:54.650
To know why a bunch of people who tried
over and over to kill each other

02:15:55.360 --> 02:15:57.320
would show up and call for peace.

02:16:16.760 --> 02:16:19.210
The story of what we've seen.

02:16:31.080 --> 02:16:33.650
Let's tell them all of it.

02:16:55.380 --> 02:16:59.130
Eren, the others are coming to visit soon.

02:17:02.680 --> 02:17:04.160
Doesn't that make you happy?

02:17:45.720 --> 02:17:50.010
I want to see you again.

02:18:13.010 --> 02:18:18.210
Eren, thanks for wrapping
this scarf around me.

02:22:08.990 --> 02:22:10.800
It's over...

02:22:10.800 --> 02:22:11.840
Yeah.

02:22:12.520 --> 02:22:13.800
What'd you think?

02:22:13.800 --> 02:22:15.280
Hmm...

02:22:15.700 --> 02:22:18.050
I liked it.

02:22:18.050 --> 02:22:22.910
It was a really long story,
but all the foreshadowing paid off,

02:22:23.490 --> 02:22:27.080
and we got to say a proper goodbye
to all the characters.

02:22:27.700 --> 02:22:31.580
Yeah... You don't read
the theory sites, Mikasa.

02:22:32.070 --> 02:22:36.260
I think my dark comrade said something, but
I couldn't hear, because he didn't speak up.

02:22:36.260 --> 02:22:38.340
There were still mysteries left hanging!

02:22:38.620 --> 02:22:41.690
It's like... It's pretty much what I expected,

02:22:41.690 --> 02:22:46.770
but I figured there'd be something that
betrayed my expectations, in a good way!

02:22:47.780 --> 02:22:49.250
Well...

02:22:49.250 --> 02:22:53.490
I think it's reasonable to say that they
left some things open to interpretation!

02:22:53.840 --> 02:22:56.400
Or that they wanted it to
have a nice, simple ending!

02:22:56.400 --> 02:23:00.770
Sometimes it's easier to like someone
if they have flaws, right?

02:23:00.770 --> 02:23:01.820
Sometimes...

02:23:01.820 --> 02:23:06.040
Those words aren't enough to erase
my doubts and dissatisfaction!

02:23:06.390 --> 02:23:12.260
Because I've been waiting
for this day... for ten years!

02:23:14.590 --> 02:23:16.150
Let's hear what Eren has to say!

02:23:16.150 --> 02:23:17.930
It wasn't that bad, right?

02:23:22.440 --> 02:23:23.940
I...

02:23:28.780 --> 02:23:31.690
I was happy I got to see
the movie with you guys.

02:23:32.640 --> 02:23:36.980
If there's a sequel or something,
let's go see it together.

02:23:46.220 --> 02:23:51.910
It's hard to believe, though, right? That these
Titans really existed a hundred years ago.

02:23:51.910 --> 02:23:55.780
I don't know how much of it was
based on actual history, though.

02:23:55.780 --> 02:24:00.300
I hope those three childhood friends
really existed.

02:24:00.300 --> 02:24:02.420
Yeah, me too.
